      "title": "Search Page",
      "description": "Search Page Home Why EKU Equal Opportunity & Title IX Benefits Contact Applicant Login Kiosk mode Welcome to Eastern Kentucky University's Careers! At EKU, we are a school of opportunity. We create and sustain a workplace culture of excellence and high engagement, foster innovation, and growth, promote respect, and support the integration of the demands of work and life. Come join us in our mission! Skip to jobs search results Category Search categories 20 filter options found Category Academic Support Positions (4 items) 4 Administrative Support Positions (3 items) 3 Arlington (3 items) 3 Athletics Positions (10 items) 10 College of Business (8 items) 8 College of Education & Applied Human Sciences (3 items) 3 College of Health Sciences (5 items) 5 College of Justice, Safety & Military Science (15 items) 15 College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sciences (18 items) 18 College of Science, Tech, Eng & Math (20 items) 20 Financial Positions (3 items) 3 Hospitality Positions (2 items) 2 Maintenance Positions (1 items) 1 Management Positions (2 items) 2 Marketing Positions (1 items) 1 Model Lab School Positions (2 items) 2 Protective Services Positions (Police) (1 items) 1 Skilled Craft Positions (9 items) 9 Student Support Positions (81 items) 81 Technology Positions (2 items) 2 Employment Type Search employment types 9 filter options found Employment Type Fulltime Administrator (1 items) 1 Fulltime Faculty (9 items) 9 Fulltime Staff (38 items) 38 Graduate Assistant (4 items) 4 Model Staff & Faculty (2 items) 2 Part-Time Faculty (29 items) 29 Part-Time Staff (13 items) 13 Seasonal or Temporary (6 items) 6 Student (71 items) 71 City Search cities 3 filter options found City Other EKU Location (6 items) 6 Remote Opportunities (8 items) 8 Richmond Campus (156 items) 156 Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Graphic Design Studio Assistant 497735 Richmond Campus College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sciences Student Support Positions Student The EKU School of Art and Design is seeking a dependable and organized student worker to assist with the day-to-day needs of the Graphic Design program. Read more Student Assistant 497732 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Student Assistant will staff the College Advising Office front desk, where they will schedule appointments for academic advisors, assist with basic advising questions, and direct visitors throughout the building.  Student Assistant will assist with direct recruitment initiatives, including but not limited to building tours, emails to prospective students, direct mail efforts, etc. Read more Coordinator, Graduate Education 497611 Richmond Campus Academic Support Positions Fulltime Staff Provides professional high level administrative support to graduate students, faculty, and staff by preparing reports, processing graduate student record requests, performing support functions such as preparing correspondence, receiving visitors, arranging conference calls and scheduling in-person meetings, creating, and sending communications, presenting to undergraduate and graduate student groups, and scheduling meetings. Will also train and provide technical direction to lower-level clerical staff. Read more USAC Ambassador Education Abroad Student Worker 497657 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student The Education Abroad Office is looking for an outgoing student worker with study abroad experience through USAC, who is interested in sharing their experience and supporting the office and other students in their efforts to study abroad. Read more Specialist, Education & Career 497729 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Fulltime Staff The Education and Career Specialist for the Appalachian Heartlands Talent Search  program at Eastern Kentucky University (EKU) provides academic, career, and financial guidance to help potential first-generation and income-eligible students successfully enter and complete postsecondary education. Read more Associate Director, Educational Talent Search 497726 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Fulltime Staff The Associate Director of Appalachian Heartlands Talent Search at Eastern Kentucky University (EKU) supports the program director in managing a federally funded TRIO project that helps middle school, high school, and adult learners from disadvantaged backgrounds pursue higher education. Read more Undergraduate Research Assistant Positions: Joshi Lab 497731 Richmond Campus College of Science, Tech, Eng & Math Student Join a funded research project investigating how bioactive compounds could be used to prevent blood clots and treat cardiovascular disease. Read more Tennis Assistant 497710 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Candidate will assist with clinics, maintain the daily schedule of the tennis center, which included seasonal rented courts, as well as EKU practice times for the tennis teams. Read more Education Abroad Student Worker 497656 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student The Education Abroad Office is looking for an outgoing student worker, preferably with study abroad experience, who is interested in sharing their experience and supporting the office and other students in their efforts to study abroad here at EKU. Read more Student Government Association Stipend Position 497724 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student This position is for administrative SGA positions that are held at the stipend level. Read more Adventure Programs Student Staff 497549 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Adventure Programs is looking for people who have climbing wall and challenge course experience, or the desire to be taught job skills in these areas. Individuals need to be dependable, trustworthy and have a positive personality. Read more Art & Design Model 497723 Richmond Campus College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sciences Student Support Positions Seasonal or Temporary Student MODELS NEEDED Drawing & Painting Class. Art & Design is looking for a few good models for studio classes that study the human figure. Read more EMC Lab Student Worker 497722 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Student worker position intended to supplement the on-campus EMT and paramedic skills laboratory classes. Read more Specialist, Post-Award Grants 497601 Richmond Campus Academic Support Positions Fulltime Staff The Post-Award Specialist is responsible for contract negotiation for sponsored projects and post award administrative tasks including budget development support, communicating pre- and post-award compliance concerns, processing award modifications and prior approval requests, providing post-award training and technical assistance to project directors, and completing special projects as assigned to meet the needs of the University and the Sponsored Programs and Research Administration office. Read more STEM Center Learning Assistant 497668 Richmond Campus College of Science, Tech, Eng & Math Student The Center for STEM Excellence at Eastern Kentucky University seeks to hire students from any major as Learning Assistants for Fall 2026. Read more Aviation Student Worker- Dispatch 497721 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Student Flight Line Dispatcher Read more Strategist, Marketing 497690 Richmond Campus Marketing Positions Fulltime Staff The Marketing Strategist develops, implements, and optimizes data-driven marketing strategies in support of EKU's institutional priorities, including enrollment, brand, academic programs, and student success. Reporting to the Sr. Director of Strategy and Creative, this position ensures marketing initiatives are targeted, measurable, and aligned with institutional goals. The Marketing Strategist executes audience segmentation, campaign performance analysis, and multi-channel marketing strategy — including content and copywriting — to drive engagement and conversion across key audiences. Read more Associate Vice President, Enrollment Management 497715 Richmond Campus Management Positions Fulltime Staff The Associate Vice President for Enrollment Management is EKU's senior operating officer for new student enrollment across every population the institution serves. The AVP EM is accountable for delivering new student headcount, net tuition revenue, and class profile targets, and for the operational systems that convert interest into enrolled students.\n\nThe portfolio pairs recruitment across all populations with financial aid strategy and administration. That pairing is deliberate. At a regional comprehensive serving high concentrations of first-generation, rural, transfer, and adult students, award timing and affordability clarity are yield levers, not back-office functions. Separating them from recruitment produces exactly the handoff friction that loses students between admit and enroll.\n\nThis is an outcomes role. The successful candidate is an enrollment operations executive who can hold a funnel target and run a Title IV compliance shop with equal seriousness. Read more College & Career Peer Mentor 497714 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Working alongside College Enrollment & Career Counselors (CECCs) and career professionals, Peer Mentors serve as a bridge between students and their academic college. They share their firsthand EKU experiences, provide peer-to-peer guidance, assist with career readiness appointments and activities, and represent their college at recruitment and student engagement events. Read more Vivarium Technician 497716 Richmond Campus College of Science, Tech, Eng & Math Student Student will receive hands on experience caring for various animals housed in the Vivarium. Read more Assistant Curator 497717 Richmond Campus College of Science, Tech, Eng & Math Student Student assistance needed for mounting, digitizing, sorting and preparing duplicates for exchange, processing exchanged specimens, and filing of herbarium specimens. Read more Colonels Cupboard Student Worker 497713 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student The Colonels Cupboard & Closet Student Worker supports the university's efforts to address food insecurity and promote professional readiness among EKU students. Read more Assistant Director, Sports Medicine Men's Basketball 497683 Richmond Campus Athletics Positions Fulltime Staff The Sports Medicine Trainer for Men's Basketball is responsible for the prevention, evaluation, treatment, and rehabilitation of athletic injuries for student-athletes in the men's basketball program. This position works closely with team physicians, coaching staff, strength and conditioning coaches, and other sports medicine personnel to ensure the health, safety, and optimal performance of all team members throughout the year-round training and competition calendar. Read more Undergraduate Research Assistant 497707 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student The undergraduate student will assist the Department Chair, Faculty Member with literature searches, data collection and coding, report and article writing, and presentations for professional audiences around topics related to policing, victimization, and violence prevention. Read more Equipment Checkout Lab Worker 497708 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Staff the School of Communication video production checkout lab. Check out equipment to authorized students, maintain and clean equipment, labs and computers. Read more Student Lab Assistant - Engineering & Technology 497698 Richmond Campus College of Science, Tech, Eng & Math Student The EKU Department of Engineering and Technology seeks an Institutional Work Study Student Lab Assistant supporting the department's laboratories, equipment and working spaces. Position begins Fall 2026, with options to renew as needed. Engineering and Technology majors are encouraged to apply. Read more Chemical Storage Student Laboratory Assistant 497699 Richmond Campus College of Science, Tech, Eng & Math Student The EKU College of Science, Technology, Engineering, and Mathematics is accepting applications for a Student Laboratory Assistant in the Chemical Storage Facility for the 2026-2027 Academic Year, with option to renew, depending on shift availability and funding. Position pays $12/hour. Must be be enrolled at EKU and eligible for EKU student employment. Read more Director of Player Development Baseball 497706 Richmond Campus Athletics Positions Part-Time Staff Responsible for the coordination of day-to-day individual player development plans. \nAssist Head Coach in planning weekly schedules for training.\nManage and log Countable Athletics Related Activities in ARMS for NCAA compliance.\nCoordinate collection of data for analytical applications Read more Undergraduate Research Assistant - Biological Sciences 497702 Richmond Campus College of Health Sciences Student The Department of Biological Sciences is seeking a motivated and reliable undergraduate student researcher, starting Fall 2026, to work with a departmental faculty member involving hands-on laboratory tasks.  This position is 10 to 20 hours per week for the 2026-2027 academic year, renewable as needed. Flexible hours available during the academic year. Read more Interpreter III 497680 Richmond Campus Academic Support Positions Student Support Positions Fulltime Staff A Staff Interpreter facilitates communication between persons who are deaf/hard of hearing and all aspects of the public and private sector, which may include, but are not limited to, academic, business, and other entities as\nneeded and appropriate. Read more Displaying 1 - 30 of 170 in total ‹ 1 2 3 4 5 6 › Equal Opportunity Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, and/or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts, or in any employment policy or practice. Any complaint arising by reason of alleged discrimination should be directed to the Office of Equal Opportunity & Title IX, Eastern Kentucky University, Jones Bldg. Room 416, Richmond, Kentucky 40475 (859) 622-8020 , or the Assistant Secretary for Civil Rights, U.S. Department of Education, Office for Civil Rights, Lyndon Baines Johnson Department of Education Building, 400 Maryland Avenue, SW, Washington, DC. 20202 1-800-421-3481(V) , 1-800-877-8339 (TTY) . Categories About Us | Contact Us | Contribute | Privacy Policy Copyright © All Rights Reserved by Eastern Kentucky University . Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept"
