    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/graphic-design-studio-assistant-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Graphic Design Studio Assistant",
      "description": "Graphic Design Studio Assistant - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Home Why EKU Equal Opportunity & Title IX Benefits Contact Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Graphic Design Studio Assistant 497735 Richmond Campus College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sciences Student Support Positions Student Closing at: Dec 3 2026 - 23:55 EST Add to favorites View favorites Title: Graphic Design Studio Assistant Position Type: Student Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 21R010 - College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sci Division: 2R0000 - Academic Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver Hours Per Week: 10 Posted Salary Grade: Minimum $8 an hour Contact Person: Rachel Moser Job Summary/Basic Functions The EKU School of Art and Design is seeking a dependable and organized student worker to assist with the day-to-day needs of the Graphic Design program. The student worker will help maintain Graphic Design classrooms and labs, organize supplies and materials, assist with basic printing and production tasks, and provide general support to Graphic Design faculty. Primary Responsibilities • Organize and maintain Graphic Design classrooms, labs, supply areas, cabinets, and shared workspaces. • Put away, organize, and restock incoming supplies and materials. • Monitor commonly used supplies and notify faculty when materials are running low. • Pick up and deliver supplies, packages, print materials, documents, and other items from campus offices as needed. • Assist with basic printing when faculty are unavailable. • Complete basic trimming, mounting, assembly, and other production tasks as assigned. • Help prepare classrooms and workspaces for projects, critiques, workshops, recruitment activities, and special events. • Assist with hanging, removing, and organizing student work, bulletin boards, displays, and signage. • Help organize paper, mounting materials, cutting supplies, samples, archived student work, promotional materials, and program resources. • Assist with basic Graphic Design Lab organization and equipment upkeep. • Help clean, organize, and reset shared spaces after projects and events. • Assist Graphic Design faculty with other program-support tasks as needed. Minimum Qualifications Education: • Current EKU student in good academic standing. • Graphic Design or Art and Design coursework is preferred but not required. • Completion of DES 250: Introduction to Graphic Design or other Graphic Design coursework is a plus, but not required. Preferred Qualifications: • Dependable, organized, and able to work independently. • Comfortable completing a variety of organizational, production, and general support tasks. • Able to communicate professionally with faculty, students, and campus offices. • Attention to detail and willingness to maintain clean and organized shared workspaces. Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Similar Jobs Graphic Design Studio Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 21R010 - College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sci The EKU School of Art and Design is seeking a dependable and organized student worker to assist with the day-to-day needs of the Graphic Design program. Student Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 25R000 - Justice, Safety & Military Science Student Assistant will staff the College Advising Office front desk, where they will schedule appointments for academic advisors, assist with basic advising questions, and direct visitors throughout the building.  Student Assistant will assist with direct recruitment initiatives, including but not limited to building tours, emails to prospective students, direct mail efforts, etc. Coordinator, Graduate Education Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 39R000 - Graduate Education & Research Admin Provides professional high level administrative support to graduate students, faculty, and staff by preparing reports, processing graduate student record requests, performing support functions such as preparing correspondence, receiving visitors, arranging conference calls and scheduling in-person meetings, creating, and sending communications, presenting to undergraduate and graduate student groups, and scheduling meetings. Will also train and provide technical direction to lower-level clerical staff. USAC Ambassador Education Abroad Student Worker Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 20R000 - Office of the Provost The Education Abroad Office is looking for an outgoing student worker with study abroad experience through USAC, who is interested in sharing their experience and supporting the office and other students in their efforts to study abroad. Specialist, Education & Career Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 77G010 - Student Affairs-Restricted Funds The Education and Career Specialist for the Appalachian Heartlands Talent Search  program at Eastern Kentucky University (EKU) provides academic, career, and financial guidance to help potential first-generation and income-eligible students successfully enter and complete postsecondary education. Associate Director, Educational Talent Search Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 77G010 - Student Affairs-Restricted Funds The Associate Director of Appalachian Heartlands Talent Search at Eastern Kentucky University (EKU) supports the program director in managing a federally funded TRIO project that helps middle school, high school, and adult learners from disadvantaged backgrounds pursue higher education. Equal Opportunity Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, and/or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts, or in any employment policy or practice. Any complaint arising by reason of alleged discrimination should be directed to the Office of Equal Opportunity & Title IX, Eastern Kentucky University, Jones Bldg. Room 416, Richmond, Kentucky 40475 (859) 622-8020 , or the Assistant Secretary for Civil Rights, U.S. Department of Education, Office for Civil Rights, Lyndon Baines Johnson Department of Education Building, 400 Maryland Avenue, SW, Washington, DC. 20202 1-800-421-3481(V) , 1-800-877-8339 (TTY) . Categories About Us | Contact Us | Contribute | Privacy Policy Copyright © All Rights Reserved by Eastern Kentucky University . Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept"
