    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/student-assistant-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Student Assistant",
      "description": "Student Assistant - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Home Why EKU Equal Opportunity & Title IX Benefits Contact Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Student Assistant 497732 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Closing at: Dec 2 2026 - 23:55 EST Add to favorites View favorites Title: Student Assistant Position Type: Student Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 25R000 - Justice, Safety & Military Science Division: 2R0000 - Academic Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver FLSA: Non-Exempt Schedule Type: Part Time, No Benefits (less than 20 hrs per week) Hours Per Week: Up to 20 Posted Salary Grade: $9.00 per hour Contact Person: Patti Matthews Job Summary/Basic Functions Student Assistant needed for the College of Justice, Safety & Military Science. Student Assistant will staff the College Advising Office front desk, where they will schedule appointments for academic advisors, assist with basic advising questions, and direct visitors throughout the building. Student Assistant will also assist with standard office duties related to filing, copies, and organization. Student Assistant will also assist with college-sponsored events, including event setup and cleanup, moving tables, chairs, etc.; data entry; research; social media; and other duties as assigned. Student Assistant will assist with direct recruitment initiatives, including but not limited to building tours, emails to prospective students, direct mail efforts, etc. The ability to work independently and deal with the public is inherent to the position. An outgoing personality with strong organizational skills and attention to detail are required. Student Assistant must be able to lift/move boxes and other materials and may also be required to work occasional evenings or weekends (with prior notice) in support of college-related events. College of Justice, Safety & Military Science major is strongly preferred. Position is funded by Federal Work Study Funds. Institutional Funding is not available for this position. Minimum Qualifications Currently enrolled EKU student in good academic standing. Minimum 2.5 cumulative GPA. Strong interpersonal and written/verbal communication skills. Demonstrated professionalism, reliability, and ability to work independently. Genuine interest in helping fellow students and prospective students. Willingness to learn and accurately communicate information about the assigned academic college and EKU resources. Ability to maintain confidentiality and follow FERPA requirements. Ability to attend required training and scheduled events. Preferred Qualifications: Assisting with college-sponsored events, mailings, data entry, clerical duties, cleaning/organizing, and other duties as assigned. Student Assistant must have a working knowledge of Word, Excel, Outlook, and other common software programs and social media platforms. An outgoing personality, dependability, promptness, confidentiality, strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and being a self-starter are required. Students must also be able to lift/move boxes and have reliable transportation. Occasional events/weekends (with prior notice) may be required. Job Duties: 40% - Assisting with Advising Office - (Essential) 30% - Assisting with recruitment events/duties - (Essential) 20% - Assisting with office/clerical duties - (Essential) 10% - Other duties as assigned - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Open Until Filled: Yes EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 7fdecbc2 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 25R000 - Justice, Safety & Military Science 25R000 - Justice, Safety & Military Science Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) 172d73d6 Last Name (required) b571f573 Email (required) 31f0b8b2 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graphic Design Studio Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 21R010 - College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sci The EKU School of Art and Design is seeking a dependable and organized student worker to assist with the day-to-day needs of the Graphic Design program. Student Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 25R000 - Justice, Safety & Military Science Student Assistant will staff the College Advising Office front desk, where they will schedule appointments for academic advisors, assist with basic advising questions, and direct visitors throughout the building.  Student Assistant will assist with direct recruitment initiatives, including but not limited to building tours, emails to prospective students, direct mail efforts, etc. Coordinator, Graduate Education Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 39R000 - Graduate Education & Research Admin Provides professional high level administrative support to graduate students, faculty, and staff by preparing reports, processing graduate student record requests, performing support functions such as preparing correspondence, receiving visitors, arranging conference calls and scheduling in-person meetings, creating, and sending communications, presenting to undergraduate and graduate student groups, and scheduling meetings. Will also train and provide technical direction to lower-level clerical staff. USAC Ambassador Education Abroad Student Worker Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 20R000 - Office of the Provost The Education Abroad Office is looking for an outgoing student worker with study abroad experience through USAC, who is interested in sharing their experience and supporting the office and other students in their efforts to study abroad. Specialist, Education & Career Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 77G010 - Student Affairs-Restricted Funds The Education and Career Specialist for the Appalachian Heartlands Talent Search  program at Eastern Kentucky University (EKU) provides academic, career, and financial guidance to help potential first-generation and income-eligible students successfully enter and complete postsecondary education. Associate Director, Educational Talent Search Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 77G010 - Student Affairs-Restricted Funds The Associate Director of Appalachian Heartlands Talent Search at Eastern Kentucky University (EKU) supports the program director in managing a federally funded TRIO project that helps middle school, high school, and adult learners from disadvantaged backgrounds pursue higher education. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 1dd0f0c1 Last Name (required) 7f411507 Email (required) 6f3542af Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Equal Opportunity Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, and/or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts, or in any employment policy or practice. Any complaint arising by reason of alleged discrimination should be directed to the Office of Equal Opportunity & Title IX, Eastern Kentucky University, Jones Bldg. Room 416, Richmond, Kentucky 40475 (859) 622-8020 , or the Assistant Secretary for Civil Rights, U.S. Department of Education, Office for Civil Rights, Lyndon Baines Johnson Department of Education Building, 400 Maryland Avenue, SW, Washington, DC. 20202 1-800-421-3481(V) , 1-800-877-8339 (TTY) . Categories About Us | Contact Us | Contribute | Privacy Policy Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by Eastern Kentucky University . Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
