      "description": "USAC Ambassador Education Abroad Student Worker - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Home Why EKU Equal Opportunity & Title IX Benefits Contact Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! USAC Ambassador Education Abroad Student Worker 497657 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Closing at: Nov 4 2026 - 23:55 EST Add to favorites View favorites Title: USAC Ambassador Education Abroad Student Worker Position Type: Student Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 20R000 - Office of the Provost Division: 2R0000 - Academic Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver FLSA: Non-Exempt Hours Per Week: 10 Additional Schedule Details: Fall 2026 Posted Salary Grade: Minimum $8.00/hour Contact Person: Katie Samuel Job Summary/Basic Functions This student position is for employment in the Education Abroad Office. The Student Employee will be greeting students, filing, working on special projects as assigned, and a variety of clerical duties. This position is also responsible for promoting USAC programs in addition to the standard duties assigned to student workers. Minimum Qualifications Education: Must be enrolled at EKU Experience: Must have some experience with study abroad. Preferred Qualifications: Creative experience designing posters and flyers and working knowledge of social media platforms is a plus. Strong organizational skills and knowledge base in Microsoft Office products is preferred. Job Duties: 34% - Promoting Study Abroad - (Essential) 33% - Filing - (Essential) 33% - Peer Advising - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Grant Open Until Filled: No EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, na