    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/specialist-education-career-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Specialist, Education & Career",
      "description": "Specialist, Education & Career - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Home Why EKU Equal Opportunity & Title IX Benefits Contact Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Specialist, Education & Career 497729 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Fulltime Staff Add to favorites View favorites Title: Specialist, Education & Career Position Type: Fulltime Staff Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 77G010 - Student Affairs-Restricted Funds Division: 5G0000 - Student Success, Engage & Opp-Restr Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: University Driver FLSA: Exempt Schedule Type: Full Time (37.5 hrs per week or more) Hours Per Week: Additional Schedule Details: May require overnight and weekend duties. Posted Salary Grade: Exempt - G19 Retirement: KTRS Contact Person: Andrea Brin Job Summary/Basic Functions The Education and Career Specialist for the Appalachian Heartlands Talent Search program at Eastern Kentucky University (EKU) provides academic, career, and financial guidance to help potential first-generation and income-eligible students successfully enter and complete postsecondary education. Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor’s degree in education, counseling, social work, or a related field required. Experience: One year of experience is required. Experience working with underrepresented, first-generation, or low-income youth (experience in rural school districts preferred). Experience with data entry systems and maintaining detailed compliance records. Excellent communication, public speaking, and organizational skills. Proficiency in MS Office and database management. Individuals who have succeeded in overcoming barriers similar to those confronting the target population (e.g., first-generation college graduates) are strongly encouraged to apply. Licensure & Certifications: Preferred Qualifications: Job Duties: 60% - Program Service Delivery Academic & Career Advising: Provide individual and group advising on high school graduation requirements, college admissions, career exploration, and financial literacy. Workshops & Events: Plan and facilitate workshops on ACT/SAT preparation, scholarship searches, and completing the FAFSA (Free Application for Federal Student Aid). Campus, Career & Experiential Visits: Coordinate and chaperone college campus visits, career fairs, and enrichment activities. - (Essential) 20% - Administrative Duties & Data Entry Meticulous Record-Keeping: Maintain accurate, highly organized, and confidential student files in compliance with federal regulations and FERPA. Data Entry: Promptly and accurately enter participant demographics, eligibility documentation, and services provided into the program's student tracking database (e.g., Blumen, TDS, or similar database). - (Essential) 15% - Recruitment & Outreach Identify and Recruit: Actively recruit eligible middle and high school students to meet annual program enrollment goals set by the U.S. Department of Education. School & Community Relations: Build and maintain strong, collaborative relationships with school counselors, teachers, administrators, and parents in the target area. Promotional Presentations: Design and deliver engaging presentations to students, families, and community stakeholders about the benefits of the TRIO Talent Search program. - (Essential) 5% - Other Duties Professional Development: Attend regional/national TRIO conferences, training sessions, and institutional meetings to stay current on federal regulations and college access best practices. Program Collaboration: Assist with other TRIO-related activities, target area and campus-wide initiatives, and community events as needed to promote student success and the TRIO Talent Search Program. Adaptable Support: Perform other program-related duties as assigned by the Program Director/Associate Director to support the overall goals and objectives of the grant. - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Grant Open Until Filled: Yes Special Instructions: EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert b2281bdf Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 77G010 - Student Affairs-Restricted Funds 77G010 - Student Affairs-Restricted Funds Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) f1c94ee3 Last Name (required) 9df9aafd Email (required) 409904b1 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graphic Design Studio Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 21R010 - College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sci The EKU School of Art and Design is seeking a dependable and organized student worker to assist with the day-to-day needs of the Graphic Design program. Student Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 25R000 - Justice, Safety & Military Science Student Assistant will staff the College Advising Office front desk, where they will schedule appointments for academic advisors, assist with basic advising questions, and direct visitors throughout the building.  Student Assistant will assist with direct recruitment initiatives, including but not limited to building tours, emails to prospective students, direct mail efforts, etc. Coordinator, Graduate Education Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 39R000 - Graduate Education & Research Admin Provides professional high level administrative support to graduate students, faculty, and staff by preparing reports, processing graduate student record requests, performing support functions such as preparing correspondence, receiving visitors, arranging conference calls and scheduling in-person meetings, creating, and sending communications, presenting to undergraduate and graduate student groups, and scheduling meetings. Will also train and provide technical direction to lower-level clerical staff. USAC Ambassador Education Abroad Student Worker Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 20R000 - Office of the Provost The Education Abroad Office is looking for an outgoing student worker with study abroad experience through USAC, who is interested in sharing their experience and supporting the office and other students in their efforts to study abroad. Specialist, Education & Career Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 77G010 - Student Affairs-Restricted Funds The Education and Career Specialist for the Appalachian Heartlands Talent Search  program at Eastern Kentucky University (EKU) provides academic, career, and financial guidance to help potential first-generation and income-eligible students successfully enter and complete postsecondary education. Associate Director, Educational Talent Search Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 77G010 - Student Affairs-Restricted Funds The Associate Director of Appalachian Heartlands Talent Search at Eastern Kentucky University (EKU) supports the program director in managing a federally funded TRIO project that helps middle school, high school, and adult learners from disadvantaged backgrounds pursue higher education. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) fe5c31f1 Last Name (required) e4ead56c Email (required) 73801a1f