    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/associate-director-educational-talent-search-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Educational Talent Search",
      "description": "Associate Director, Educational Talent Search - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Home Why EKU Equal Opportunity & Title IX Benefits Contact Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Associate Director, Educational Talent Search 497726 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Fulltime Staff Add to favorites View favorites Title: Associate Director, Educational Talent Search Position Type: Fulltime Staff Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 77G010 - Student Affairs-Restricted Funds Division: 5G0000 - Student Success, Engage & Opp-Restr Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: University Driver FLSA: Exempt Schedule Type: Full Time (37.5 hrs per week or more) Hours Per Week: Additional Schedule Details: This position may require night, weekend, and overnight duties. Posted Salary Grade: Exempt - G22 Retirement: KTRS Contact Person: Andrea Brin Job Summary/Basic Functions The Associate Director of Appalachian Heartlands Talent Search at Eastern Kentucky University (EKU) supports the program director in managing a federally funded TRIO project that helps middle school, high school, and adult learners from disadvantaged backgrounds pursue higher education. Minimum Qualifications Education: Master's Degree Social Work, Education, or related field. Experience: Five years experience working in education, social work, or other related field Licensure & Certifications: Preferred Qualifications: Job Duties: 40% - Provide strategic oversight of the ETS Programming unit in daily operations to include recruitment and application review, curriculum development, curriculum facilitation, analysis of processes and increase efficiencies for meeting program objectives. - (Essential) 20% - Stay informed of higher education trends and secondary graduation requirements. Responsible for applying federal, state and university regulations to meet program objectives and compliance. Establish best practices, deliver trainings, maintai