    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/undergraduate-research-assistant-positions-joshi-lab-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Undergraduate Research Assistant Positions: Joshi Lab",
      "description": "Undergraduate Research Assistant Positions: Joshi Lab - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Home Why EKU Equal Opportunity & Title IX Benefits Contact Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Undergraduate Research Assistant Positions: Joshi Lab 497731 Richmond Campus College of Science, Tech, Eng & Math Student Closing at: Dec 1 2026 - 23:55 EST Add to favorites View favorites Title: Undergraduate Research Assistant Positions: Joshi Lab Position Type: Student Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 21R000 - Science, Tech, Engineering & Math Division: 2R0000 - Academic Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver FLSA: Non-Exempt Hours Per Week: 10 Contact Person: robert.pace@eku.edu Job Summary/Basic Functions Principal Investigator: Dr. Smita Joshi, Department of Biological Sciences Project Description: Join a funded research project investigating how bioactive compounds could be used to prevent blood clots and treat cardiovascular disease. This is a paid position and an excellent opportunity to gain hands-on experience in a biomedical research lab, contributing to work that could lead to safer, more effective therapies. Key Responsibilities: ● Assist with lab experiments, including in vitro platelet assays. ● Help with data collection and analysis. ● Conduct literature reviews and maintain detailed research records. Who We're Looking For: ● A hard-working, curious, and detail-oriented team player with a strong interest in biomedical research. ● Must have completed at least BIO 111 and BIO 112, preferably a sophomore or junior. ● No prior research experience is required; we will provide all necessary training. ● Should be available for 9–10 hours per week, with at least one continuous 4–5-hour block of time available on a single day (Mon-Thurs). What You Will Gain: ● Significant hands-on research experience to strengthen your resume for graduate or medical school. ● Skills in data analysis and scientific communication. ● Opportunities to present your research findings at scientific conferences and networking with colleagues at other institutions. How to Apply: Please submit your resume, unofficial transcript and a brief statement of interest to Dr. Smita Joshi at smita.joshi@eku.edu. In your statement, please explain why you are interested in this opportunity. Applications will be reviewed on a rolling basis until the positions are filled. We look forward to hearing from you! Minimum Qualifications Education: Must be enrolled at EKU. Licensure & Certifications: Key Responsibilities: ● Assist with lab experiments, including in vitro platelet assays. ● Help with data collection and analysis. ● Conduct literature reviews and maintain detailed research records. Who We're Looking For: ● A hard-working, curious, and detail-oriented team player with a strong interest in biomedical research. ● Must have completed at least BIO 111 and BIO 112, preferably a sophomore or junior. ● No prior research experience is required; we will provide all necessary training. ● Should be available for 9–10 hours per week, with at least one continuous 4–5-hour block of time available on a single day (Mon-Thurs). Preferred Qualifications: Job Duties: Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: No EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign 