    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/emc-lab-student-worker-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "We're Hiring!",
      "description": "EMC Lab Student Worker - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Home Why EKU Equal Opportunity & Title IX Benefits Contact Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! EMC Lab Student Worker 497722 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Closing at: Nov 27 2026 - 23:55 EST Add to favorites View favorites Title: EMC Lab Student Worker Position Type: Student Search Type: External - Minimum 7 days Department: 25R000 - Justice, Safety & Military Science Division: 2R0000 - Academic Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver Schedule Type: Part Time, No Benefits (less than 20 hrs per week) Hours Per Week: 10-15 Additional Schedule Details: Must have availability for at least two of the lab meeting days: EMC 110: TR 9:30am-12:45pm EMC 110: MW 9:05 am-12:20pm EMC 342: M 3:45pm-6:45pm EMC 342: W 3:45pm-6:45pm Posted Salary Grade: $16.25/hr Retirement: None Contact Person: Dr. Bill Young Job Summary/Basic Functions This is a student worker position intended to supplement the on-campus EMT and paramedic skills laboratory classes. Qualified applicants must have the aptitude for teaching and explaining skills to students in initial certification-level courses at the EMT-Basic and/or paramedic level. Preference will be given to students who are licensed paramedics capable of assisting both levels of lab classes. This is intended for full-time undergraduate or graduate students who qualify for institutional work study. Minimum Qualifications Must submit proof of NREMT and/or state-level EMT or paramedic certification. Must have desire to teach/mentor students in clinical settings; preference given to those with FTO experience, precepting experience, and/or instructor/tutoring experience. Must submit proof of current class schedule to prove eligibility to work during lab times. Must be a full-time student at EKU. Preferred Qualifications: Kentucky or NREMT Licensed EMT Required Kentucky or NREMT Licensed Paramedic desired Job Duties: 50% - Assist current EMC 110L/EMC 342 instructors in maintaining an appropriate instructor-to-student ratio per state regulatory regulations. - (Essential) 25% - Assist in maintenance and organization of EMT Basic and paramedic skills labs in various tasks as directed by faculty. - (Essential) 15% - Offer available times to work with EMT/paramedic students for tutoring and mentorship. - (Essential) 10% - Offer available times to work with faculty regarding academic or departmental activities and research - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Open Until Filled: Yes EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 16ea0618 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 25R000 - Justice, Safety & Military Science 25R000 - Justice, Safety & Military Science Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) 97979eb9 Last Name (required) 5d477995 Email (required) c11c67a7 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graphic Design Studio Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 21R010 - College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sci The EKU School of Ar