    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/stem-center-learning-assistant-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states-51b53a85-2644-413e-bef4-30df6f7b7402": {
      "title": "STEM Center Learning Assistant",
      "description": "STEM Center Learning Assistant - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Home Why EKU Equal Opportunity & Title IX Benefits Contact Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! STEM Center Learning Assistant 497668 Richmond Campus College of Science, Tech, Eng & Math Student Closing at: Sep 30 2026 - 23:55 EDT Add to favorites View favorites Title: STEM Center Learning Assistant Position Type: Student Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 20R000 - Office of the Provost Division: 2R0000 - Academic Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver FLSA: Non-Exempt Hours Per Week: 5-20 Contact Person: Judith Jenkins Job Summary/Basic Functions The Center for STEM Excellence at Eastern Kentucky University seeks to hire students from any major as Learning Assistants. Learning Assistants (LAs) will support student learning in science, technology, engineering, and mathematics (STEM) courses. LAs work on-campus with students one-on-one, in small groups, and may facilitate workshops on problem-solving strategies, study skills, exam preparation, and related topics. Some LAs may be assigned up to three sections of an undergraduate STEM lecture or laboratory course and will work with the instructor and STEM Center Personnel to facilitate in-class and/or out-of-class learning experiences. Specific duties will vary based on the course, the LA’s areas of expertise, and students’ learning needs. Additional duties will include active participation in weekly staff meetings, active participation in professional development workshops, and some tutoring in their preferred subject area(s). The STEM Center offers flexible scheduling to work with your course schedules. At this time, we are hiring LAs to support the following courses: Anatomy and Physiology laboratories - BIO 208 (Formerly BIO 307), BIO 308 Nursing Dosage Calculation Workshops - NSC 114, 232, 380 (No nursing background needed - a background in chemistry, math, or physics is sufficient) Algebra - MAT 112 Chemistry - CHE 105, 111, 112 Other STEM courses at the discretion of the course instructor and STEM Center staff. The Center for STEM Excellence is accepting applications for this position on an ongoing basis. Should your application be considered, you will be contacted by the hiring official. Minimum Qualifications Licensure & Certifications: Applicants must be full-time students at EKU, have completed at least one General Education II course (Quantitative Reasoning) or General Education IV course (Natural Sciences), and be in good academic standing with the University. Preferred Qualifications: A successful candidate will also possess strong understanding of 100-level course content in at least one area of science, technology, engineering, or math, an interest in cultivating student learning in STEM, strong communication skills, a passion for working with students, and the willingness to be an energetic and reliable student representative of the Center for STEM Excellence. A minimum GPA of 2.8 is preferred. Job Duties: 40% - Facilitate meaningful learning experiences (problem-solving and/or skill-building workshops, tutoring, etc.) - (Essential) 30% - Foster productive learning environments in the SCIBD Atrium and any other spaces to which you’re assigned. - (Essential) 20% - Actively participate in weekly training and professional development related to your assigned role. - (Essential) 10% - Support day-to-day STEM Center activities by completing other duties as assigned. - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Open Until Filled: No Special Instructions: Please include a copy of your resume, a cover letter explaining your interest in the position and STEM content area(s) of interest, and an unofficial copy of your transcript. Also include contact information for a minimum of one and up to two professional references. One professional reference must be an EKU instructor from your area of interest. EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert a7e65fdd Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 20R000 - Office of the Provost 20R000 - Office of the Provost Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) 660998f9 Last Name (required) 2398b6d4 Email (required) 7a540cf9 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graphic Design Studio Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 21R010 - College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sci The EKU School of Art and Design is seeking a dependable and organized student worker to assist with the day-to-day needs of the Graphic Design program. Student Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 25R000 - Justice, Safety & Military Science Student Assistant will staff the College Advising Office front desk, where they will schedule appointments for academic advisors, assist with basic advising questions, and direct visitors throughout the building.  Student Assistant will assist with direct recruitment initiatives, including but not limited to building tours, emails to prospective students, direct mail efforts, etc. Coordinator, Gradua