      "description": "Aviation Student Worker- Dispatch - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Home Why EKU Equal Opportunity & Title IX Benefits Contact Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Aviation Student Worker- Dispatch 497721 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Closing at: Nov 26 2026 - 23:55 EST Add to favorites View favorites Title: Aviation Student Worker- Dispatch Position Type: Student Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 25R000 - Justice, Safety & Military Science Division: 2R0000 - Academic Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver FLSA: Non-Exempt Schedule Type: Part Time, No Benefits (less than 20 hrs per week) Hours Per Week: 20 Posted Salary Grade: $9.25 per hour Contact Person: Shauna Smith Job Summary/Basic Functions A successful applicant will assist with daily requirements of the Aviation Program within the flight line. Duties will include assisting the flight line dispatch supervisor in every day operations. Duties for Dispatch are assigned daily by the Supervisor. Duties can include dispatching, cleaning, auditing dispatch tickets, washing aircraft, auditing aircraft or other duties as assigned. Please include the following documents. 1.Copy of student summer, fall, spring and/or winter acedemic schedule 2. Copy of resume Minimum Qualifications Must be enrolled at EKU at least 12 hours Preferred Qualifications: Proficient in Word, Excel, PowerPoint Be able to pick up on tasks rather quickly Must have a flight schedule pro account Student must have passed the private pilot checkride. Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Open Until Filled: Yes EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran sta