    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/strategist-marketing-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states-fb901b46-6509-47d4-bf58-597607af9b78": {
      "title": "We're Hiring!",
      "description": "Strategist, Marketing - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Home Why EKU Equal Opportunity & Title IX Benefits Contact Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Strategist, Marketing 497690 Richmond Campus Marketing Positions Fulltime Staff Add to favorites View favorites Title: Strategist, Marketing Position Type: Fulltime Staff Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 30R003 - StudentSuccess,Outreach&Opportunity Division: 5R0000 - Student Success, Engage & Oppor Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver FLSA: Exempt Schedule Type: Full Time (37.5 hrs per week or more) Hours Per Week: Additional Schedule Details: Posted Salary Grade: Exempt - G22 Retirement: KTRS Contact Person: Brooke Gibson Job Summary/Basic Functions The Marketing Strategist develops, implements, and optimizes data-driven marketing strategies in support of EKU's institutional priorities, including enrollment, brand, academic programs, and student success. Reporting to the Sr. Director of Strategy and Creative, this position ensures marketing initiatives are targeted, measurable, and aligned with institutional goals. The Marketing Strategist executes audience segmentation, campaign performance analysis, and multi-channel marketing strategy — including content and copywriting — to drive engagement and conversion across key audiences. Minimum Qualifications Education: Bachelor's degree in Marketing, Communications, English, Journalism, or a related field. Experience may be substituted for specific degree requirements but not educational level. Experience: Two years of experience in marketing, content development, or communications. Experience with multi-channel marketing campaigns and digital platforms preferred. Familiarity with CRM systems (Technolutions Slate preferred) a plus Licensure & Certifications: Preferred Qualifications: Job Duties: 35% - Strategic Campaign Development & Execution Develops and implements multi-channel marketing strategies integrating email, digital advertising, social media, print, and web content in support of institutional marketing priorities. Collaborates with internal stakeholders to ensure campaign messaging aligns with EKU's brand voice and strategic goals. Oversees campaign planning, timelines, execution, and performance tracking to optimize engagement and conversion rates. - (Essential) 25% - Content Development & Copywriting Writes and edits audience-specific copy for email campaigns, web pages, social media, digital advertising, print collateral, and video scripts. Ensures all written content reflects EKU's brand voice and is appropriately tailored to the target audience and channel. Partners with the creative team to ensure copy and design are developed in alignment with campaign messaging strategy. - (Essential) 20% - Audience Segmentation & Personalization Leverages Technolutions Slate and other digital marketing platforms to develop targeted campaigns tailored to distinct audience segments. Implements A/B testing, automation workflows, and behavioral triggers to enhance marketing effectiveness. Ensures campaign messaging and visuals are appropriately tailored for each segment and funnel stage. - (Essential) 15% - Performance Analytics & Optimization Tracks and analyzes marketing KPIs including click-through rates, conversions, engagement, and yield to inform decision-making. Uses Google Analytics, CRM dashboards, and reporting tools to measure and refine marketing effectiveness. Provides data-driven recommendations for campaign adjustments, messaging refinements, and budget considerations. - (Essential) 5% - Collaboration & Project Managemen Works with Admissions, Enrollment Management, Student Success, and other campus partners to ensure marketing efforts support institutional priorities. Supports project management functions including marketing calendars, deadlines, and vendor/agency coordination. - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: Yes Special Instructions: EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 6302bfff Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 30R003 - StudentSuccess,Outreach&Opportunity 30R003 - StudentSuccess,Outreach&Opportunity Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) 87f2ef86 Last Name (required) e41e68bd Email (required) e66e668a Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graphic Design Studio Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 21R010 - College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sci The EKU School of Art and Design is seeking a dependable and organized student worker to assist with the day-to-day needs of the Graphic Design program. Student Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 25R000 - Justice, Safety & Military Science Student Assistant will staff the College Advising Office front desk, where they will schedule appointments for academic advisors, assist with basic advising questions, and direct visitors throughout the building.  Student Assistant will assist with direct recruitment initiatives, includin