    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/associate-vice-president-enrollment-management-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Associate Vice President, Enrollment Management",
      "description": "Associate Vice President, Enrollment Management - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Home Why EKU Equal Opportunity & Title IX Benefits Contact Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Associate Vice President, Enrollment Management 497715 Richmond Campus Management Positions Fulltime Staff Add to favorites View favorites Title: Associate Vice President, Enrollment Management Position Type: Fulltime Staff Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 30R003 - StudentSuccess,Outreach&Opportunity Division: 5R0000 - Student Success, Engage & Oppor Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: University Driver FLSA: Exempt Schedule Type: Full Time (37.5 hrs per week or more) Hours Per Week: Additional Schedule Details: Some evenings and weekends required. Posted Salary Grade: Exempt - G29 Retirement: KTRS Contact Person: Dan Hendrickson Job Summary/Basic Functions The Associate Vice President for Enrollment Management is EKU's senior operating officer for new student enrollment across every population the institution serves. The AVP EM is accountable for delivering new student headcount, net tuition revenue, and class profile targets, and for the operational systems that convert interest into enrolled students. The portfolio pairs recruitment across all populations with financial aid strategy and administration. That pairing is deliberate. At a regional comprehensive serving high concentrations of first-generation, rural, transfer, and adult students, award timing and affordability clarity are yield levers, not back-office functions. Separating them from recruitment produces exactly the handoff friction that loses students between admit and enroll. This is an outcomes role. The successful candidate is an enrollment operations executive who can hold a funnel target and run a Title IV compliance shop with equal seriousness. Minimum Qualifications Education: Master’s degree in Higher Education Administration, Student Affairs, Counseling, Public Administration, or a related field Experience: Five years of progressive leadership experience in enrollment management, admissions, or financial aid, including at least three years supervising professional staff at the director level or above. Licensure & Certifications: Preferred Qualifications: Job Duties: 25% - Own annual and multi-year new student targets across first-time full-time, transfer, adult, online, and graduate populations. Build the goals, defend the assumptions, deliver the number. Translate the Strategic Enrollment Management Plan into an operational plan with weekly execution and named owners. Present funnel performance, variance, and corrective action to the VP's Executive Council on a defined cycle. Lead net tuition revenue forecasting and scenario modeling with Institutional Effectiveness and Research and the Budget Office. Escalate risk early. The institution can absorb bad news in September. It cannot absorb bad news at census. - (Essential) 25% - Direct undergraduate admissions operations, including application review, decision release, territory design, counselor staffing, travel strategy, and conversion accountability by territory. Direct graduate, online, adult, and transfer recruitment as a distinct operating discipline with its own funnel logic, cycle timing, and conversion standards. These populations do not respond to traditional undergraduate recruitment cadence and should not be run on it. Own the 8Kby28 online enrollment growth trajectory in partnership with Academic Affairs on program supply and Regional Campuses on delivery. Build and maintain transfer pathway and articulation strategy with KCTCS and other feeder institutions, and hold the Registrar to agreed credit evaluation turnaround standards on behalf of transfer yield. Direct dual credit, early college, and college access pipeline strategy. - (Essential) 20% - Direct financial aid strategy, including institutional aid leveraging, discount rate management, scholarship matrix design, and packaging philosophy. Model and recommend aid strategies that optimize net tuition revenue while advancing access for first-generation, rural, and Pell-eligible students. Own federal and state compliance, including Title IV administration, verification, satisfactory academic progress, return of Title IV funds, and Kentucky state aid programs. Compress time from application to award, and from award to student understanding of what they will actually pay. Partner with Big E Central on aid-related navigation, escalation pathways, and case resolution. - (Essential) 15% - Direct the Welcome Center and the full campus visit operation, including daily visits, group visits, counselor-led programming, and the visitor experience standard. Own the recruitment and yield event portfolio, including open houses, admitted student programs, transfer and adult information sessions, and regional events. Establish measurable attribution from visit and event participation to application, deposit, and matriculation. Every event carries a conversion expectation or it does not run. Ensure the visit experience delivers on the brand promise made in marketing. Visit is where recruitment marketing either earns credibility or loses it. - (Essential) 15% - Serve as the primary business owner for enrollment CRM requirements, including application workflow, decision logic, portal behavior, event registration, and funnel communication flows. Submit, prioritize, and defend requirements through the agreed intake process with the Executive Director of Enrollment Systems. Define the enrollment metrics that matter, including funnel stage definitions, conversion standards, source attribution requirements, and territory reporting needs. Enrollment Systems builds and delivers against those definitions. Both parties operate from one agreed set of numbers. Specify data governance requirements from the enrollment side, including source tagging, geographic capture, and student type classification standards, and hold operational discipline within admissions, recruitment, and aid so that data entered upstream is clean. Participate in a standing joint prioritization forum with the Executive Director of Enrollment Systems. Escalate unresolved priority conflicts to the Vice President rather than working around them. Serve as the enrollment-side counterpart to Marketing and Communications, providing audience definition, lead quality standards, and conversion accountability. Brand, creative, campaign, and media authority rests with MarCom and the Vice President. Maintain a working service partnership with the Office of the Registrar covering transfer credit evaluation, registration access for new students, and enrollment data definitions. Partner with academic deans on program-level enrollment strategy, capacity planning, and new program demand assessment. Partner with Student Success and Retention leadership so that recruitment promises match the delivered experience. Manage unit operating budgets and coordinate institutional aid budget planning with the CFO. - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: Yes Special Instructions: EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 0b349d7d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 30R003 - StudentSuccess,Outreach&Opportunity 30R003 - StudentSuccess,Outreach&Opportunity Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) 737a7c7d Last Name (required) b46d17b1 Email (required) bb905b59 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graphic Design Studio Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 21R010 - College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sci The EKU School of Art and Design is seeking a dependable and organized student worker to assist with the day-to-day needs of the Graphic Design program. Student Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 25R000 - Justice, Safety & Military Science Student Assistant will staff the College Advising Office front desk, where they will schedule appointments for academic advisors, assist with basic advising questions, and direct visitors throughout the building.  Student Assistant will assist with direct recruitment initiatives, including but not limited to building tours, emails to prospective students, direct mail efforts, etc. Coordinator, Graduate Education Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 39R000 - Graduate Education & Research Admin Provides professional high level administrative support to graduate students, faculty, and staff by preparing reports, processing graduate student record requests, performing support functions such as preparing correspondence, receiving visitors, arranging conference calls and scheduling in-person meetings, creating, and sending communications, presenting to undergraduate and graduate student groups, and scheduling meetings. Will also train and provide technical direction to lower-level clerical staff. USAC Ambassador Education Abroad Student Worker Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 20R000 - Office of the Provost The Education Abroad Office is looking for an outgoing student worker with study abroad experience through USAC, who is interested in sharing their experience and supporting the office and other students in their efforts to study abroad. Specialist, Education & Career Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 77G010 - Student Affairs-Restricted Funds The Education and Career Specialist for the Appalachian Heartlands Talent Search  program at Eastern Kentucky University (EKU) provides academic, career, and financial guidance to help potential first-generation and income-eligible students successfully enter and complete postsecondary education. Associate Director, Educational Talent Search Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 77G010 - Student Affairs-Restricted Funds The Associate Director of Appalachian Heartlands Talent Search at Eastern Kentucky University (EKU) supports the program director in managing a federally funded TRIO project that helps middle school, high school, and adult learners from disadvantaged backgrounds pursue higher education. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 9d752b17 Last Name (required) fe83b864 Email (required) a31cf78f Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Equal Opportunity Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, and/or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts, or in any employment policy or practice. Any complaint arising by reason of alleged discrimination should be directed to the Office of Equal Opportunity & Title IX, Eastern Kentucky University, Jones Bldg. Room 416, Richmond, Kentucky 40475 (859) 622-8020 , or the Assistant Secretary for Civil Rights, U.S. Department of Education, Office for Civil Rights, Lyndon Baines Johnson Department of Education Building, 400 Maryland Avenue, SW, Washington, DC. 20202 1-800-421-3481(V) , 1-800-877-8339 (TTY) . Categories About Us | Contact Us | Contribute | Privacy Policy Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by Eastern Kentucky University . Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
