    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/college-career-peer-mentor-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "We're Hiring!",
      "description": "College & Career Peer Mentor - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Home Why EKU Equal Opportunity & Title IX Benefits Contact Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! College & Career Peer Mentor 497714 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Closing at: Nov 25 2026 - 23:55 EST Add to favorites View favorites Title: College & Career Peer Mentor Position Type: Student Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Division: 5G0000 - Student Success, Engage & Opp-Restr Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver Posted Salary Grade: Minimum $11 an hour Contact Person: Tevis Milburn Job Summary/Basic Functions College & Career Peer Mentors are student representatives who help create a welcoming, informative, and career-focused experience for prospective and current EKU students, families, and campus guests. Working alongside College Enrollment & Career Counselors (CECCs) and career professionals, Peer Mentors serve as a bridge between students and their academic college. They share their firsthand EKU experiences, provide peer-to-peer guidance, assist with career readiness appointments and activities, and represent their college at recruitment and student engagement events. This position is designed for students who are enthusiastic about their college, enjoy helping others, and want to develop their own communication, leadership, career development, and professional skills. Minimum Qualifications Licensure & Certifications: Currently enrolled EKU student in good academic standing. Minimum 2.5 cumulative GPA. Strong interpersonal and written/verbal communication skills. Demonstrated professionalism, reliability, and ability to work independently. Genuine interest in helping fellow students and prospective students. Willingness to learn and accurately communicate information about the assigned academic college and EKU resources. Ability to maintain confidentiality and follow FERPA requirements. Ability to attend required training and scheduled events. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with campus involvement, student organizations, leadership, customer service, recruitment, or peer mentoring. Interest or experience in career development, recruiting, admissions, human resources, marketing, or a related field. Familiarity with resume development, interviewing, LinkedIn, or other professional development tools. Strong public speaking or presentation skills. Job Duties: 50%% - Participating in training and demonstrating proficiency in assigned career readiness services including approved resume, cover letter, mock interview, and other career readiness appointments or activities. - (Essential) 25%% - Participating in recruitment, yield, and student engagement events hosted by the academic college and Enrollment & Career Readiness, including assisting with tours and presentations for prospective students, families, and visiting groups. - (Essential) 10%% - Representing the assigned academic college in a professional and welcoming manner while providing accurate peer-level information about college programs, student experiences, and career opportunities. - (Essential) 10%% - Assisting with college outreach, promotional activities, and follow-up communications and attending related meetings and training. - (Essential) 5%% - Completing other duties as assigned related to recruitment, student engagement, career readiness, and student success. - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Open Until Filled: Yes EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 0e1d05b8 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) 7240d79b Last Name (required) 25040f37 Email (required) 9a835e89 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graphic Design Studio Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 21R010 - College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sci The EKU School of Art and Design is seeking a dependable and organized student worker to assist with the day-to-day needs of the Graphic Design program. Student Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 25R000 - Justice, Safety & Military Science Student Assistant will staff the College Advising Office front desk, where they will schedule appointments for academic advisors, assist with basic advising questions, and direct visitors throughout the building.  Student Assistant will assist with direct recruitment initiatives, including but not limited to building tours, emails to prospective students, direct mail efforts, etc. Coordinator, Graduate Education Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 39R000 - Graduate Education & Research Admin Provides professional high level administrative support to graduate students, faculty, and staff by preparing reports, processing graduate student record requests, performing support functions such as preparing correspondence, receiving visitors, arranging conference calls and scheduling in-person meetings, creating, and sending communications, presenting to undergraduate and graduate student groups, and scheduling meetings. Will also train and provide technical direction to lower-level clerical staff. USAC Ambassador Education Abroad Student Worker Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 20R000 - Office of the Provost The Education Abroad Office is looking for an outgoing student worker with study abroad experience through USAC, who is interested in sharing their experience and supporting the office and other students in their efforts to study abroad. Specialist, Education & Career Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 77G010 - Student Affairs-Restricted Funds The Education and Career Specialist for the Appalachian Heartlands Talent Search  program at Eastern Kentucky University (EKU) provides academic, career, and financial guidance to help potential first-generation and income-eligible students successfully enter and complete postsecondary education. Associate Director, Educational Talent Search Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 77G010 - Student Affairs-Restricted Funds The Associate Director of Appalachian Heartlands Talent Search at Eastern Kentucky University (EKU) supports the program director in managing a federally funded TRIO project that helps middle school, high school, and adult learners from disadvantaged backgrounds pursue higher education. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 87b27551 Last Name (required) aa2cbe7c Email (required) 112fcbda Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Equal Opportunity Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, and/or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts, or in any employment policy or practice. Any complaint arising by reason 