    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/vivarium-technician-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Vivarium Technician",
      "description": "Vivarium Technician - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Home Why EKU Equal Opportunity & Title IX Benefits Contact Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Vivarium Technician 497716 Richmond Campus College of Science, Tech, Eng & Math Student Closing at: Nov 25 2026 - 23:55 EST Add to favorites View favorites Title: Vivarium Technician Position Type: Student Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 21R000 - Science, Tech, Engineering & Math Division: 2R0000 - Academic Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver Hours Per Week: up to 20 Contact Person: Kelly Watson Job Summary/Basic Functions The Vivarium Technician is a student position responsible for supporting the daily care and well-being of the Center for Science & Environmental Education’s Ambassador Animal program. The technician will assist with feeding, cleaning and maintaining animal enclosures, monitoring animal health and behavior, maintaining appropriate environmental conditions, and keeping accurate care records. The Vivarium Technician will follow established animal care and safety protocols and communicate any concerns regarding animal health, behavior, or facility conditions to the appropriate supervisor. The position may also assist with preparing ambassador animals for educational programs, outreach events, and other Center activities. Minimum Qualifications Education: Must be enrolled at EKU. Experience: Previous experience providing direct care for animals is required. Experience may include employment, volunteer work, internships, coursework, animal husbandry, veterinary settings, wildlife rehabilitation, shelters, farms, or other comparable animal-care environments. Preferred Qualifications: This position requires reliability, attention to detail, a commitment to animal welfare, and the ability to work independently while following established care procedures. Job Duties: Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Open Until Filled: No Special Instructions: Student must have an up-to-date tetanus vaccination. EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert a95546a3 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 21R000 - Science, Tech, Engineering & Math 21R000 - Science, Tech, Engineering & Math Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) f7bb2388 Last Name (required) 3c203d37 Email (required) a24acf21 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graphic Design Studio Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 21R010 - College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sci The EKU School of Art and Design is seeking a dependable and organized student worker to assist with the day-to-day needs of the Graphic Design program. Student Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 25R000 - Justice, Safety & Military Science Student Assistant will staff the College Advising Office front desk, where they will schedule appointments for academic advisors, assist with basic advising questions, and direct visitors throughout the building.  Student Assistant will assist with direct recruitment initiatives,