    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/colonels-cupboard-student-worker-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "We're Hiring!",
      "description": "Colonels Cupboard Student Worker - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Home Why EKU Equal Opportunity & Title IX Benefits Contact Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Colonels Cupboard Student Worker 497713 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Closing at: Nov 24 2026 - 23:55 EST Add to favorites View favorites Title: Colonels Cupboard Student Worker Department: 26R100 - Ctr for Incl Excell & Global Eng Division: 5R1000 - Student Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Hours Per Week: 10 Posted Salary Grade: Minimum $8 an hour Contact Person: Martina Jackson Job Summary/Basic Functions The Colonels Cupboard & Closet Student Worker supports the university's efforts to address food insecurity and promote professional readiness among EKU students. Student workers are assigned to one or more of three program areas for the Colonels Closet, Colonels Cupboard, or Stockroom & Inventory based on program needs and student interest. This position offers hands-on experience in customer service, program operations, nutrition and career education, and inventory management, while directly supporting fellow students in accessing essential resources. Student workers may rotate between tracks depending on staffing needs, or may be assigned primarily to a single area. Minimum Qualifications Education: Enrolled as a full-time EKU student in good standing. Preferred Qualifications: - Currently enrolled as a EKU student in good academic standing. - Strong interpersonal and communication skills. - Dependable, punctual, and able to commit to a regular weekly schedule. - Comfortable interacting with the broader student population in a confidential, respectful manner. - Ability to lift and carry boxes or donation items (up to approximately 25 lbs). - Willingness to learn new systems and processes (e.g., inventory software). - No prior experience required; training provided. Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert cecb1801 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 26R100 - Ctr for Incl Excell & Global Eng 26R100 - Ctr for Incl Excell & Global Eng Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) 347326d7 Last Name (required) 441783d4 Email (required) c8efa41b Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graphic Design Studio Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 21R010 - College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sci The EKU School of Art and Design is seeking a dependable and organized student worker to assist with the day-to-day needs of the Graphic Design program. Student Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 25R000 - Justice, Safety & Military Science Student Assistant will staff the College Advising Office front desk, where they will schedule appointments for academic advisors, assist with basic advising questions, and direct visitors throughout the building.  Student Assistant will assist with direct recruitment initiatives, including but not limited to building tours, emails to prospective students, direct mail efforts, etc. Coordinator, Gradu