    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/assistant-director-sports-medicine-men-s-basketball-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Sports Medicine Men's Basketball",
      "description": "Assistant Director, Sports Medicine Men's Basketball - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Home Why EKU Equal Opportunity & Title IX Benefits Contact Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Assistant Director, Sports Medicine Men's Basketball 497683 Richmond Campus Athletics Positions Fulltime Staff Add to favorites View favorites Title: Assistant Director, Sports Medicine Men's Basketball Position Type: Fulltime Staff Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 90R000 - Intercollegiate Athletics Division: 6R1000 - Intercollegiate Athletics Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: University Driver FLSA: Exempt Schedule Type: Full Time (37.5 hrs per week or more) Posted Salary Grade: Exempt - G23 Retirement: KTRS Contact Person: Dusty Ridner Job Summary/Basic Functions The Sports Medicine Trainer for Men's Basketball is responsible for the prevention, evaluation, treatment, and rehabilitation of athletic injuries for student-athletes in the men's basketball program. This position works closely with team physicians, coaching staff, strength and conditioning coaches, and other sports medicine personnel to ensure the health, safety, and optimal performance of all team members throughout the year-round training and competition calendar. Minimum Qualifications Education: A Master's Degree is required. Experience: Three years or more of experience in collegiate athletic training. Licensure & Certifications: BOC National Certification required. A State Board of Medical Licensure Certification in Athletic Training is required. A Kentucky Board of Medical Licensure Athletic Training Certification Is Preferred. The successful applicant will obtain a Kentucky Board of Medical Licensure within 3 months if not held at hire. Valid state driver's license is required. Job Duties: 40% - Provide comprehensive athletic training services, including injury prevention, evaluation, immediate care, treatment, and rehabilitation for men's basketball student-athletes. - (Essential) 30% - Attend and provide on-site medical coverage for all practices, home games, and away competitions, including travel with the team as required. Develop and implement individualized rehabilitation and return-to-play protocols in coordination with team physicians. - (Essential) 20% - Perform pre-participation physical exams and maintain compliance with NCAA medical clearance and eligibility requirements. Maintain accurate and confidential medical records, injury reports, and treatment documentation in compliance with HIPAA/FERPA regulations. Coordinate referrals to physicians, orthopedic specialists, and other healthcare providers as needed. - (Essential) 10% - Ensure full compliance with NCAA bylaws related to sports medicine, including medical hardship waivers, drug testing protocols, and student-athlete health and safety standards. Stay current on best practices, continuing education requirements, and certification renewals. Assist with budgeting and procurement of medical supplies and equipment for the basketball program. - (Essential) Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: Yes EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert c592a4fb Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each