    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/student-lab-assistant-engineering-technology-richmond-campus-kentucky-united-states": {
      "title": "Student Lab Assistant",
      "description": "Student Lab Assistant - Engineering & Technology - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Home Why EKU Equal Opportunity & Title IX Benefits Contact Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Student Lab Assistant - Engineering & Technology 497698 Richmond Campus College of Science, Tech, Eng & Math Student Closing at: Oct 19 2026 - 23:55 EDT Add to favorites View favorites Title: Student Lab Assistant - Engineering & Technology Position Type: Student Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 21R000 - Science, Tech, Engineering & Math Division: 2R0000 - Academic Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver FLSA: Non-Exempt Schedule Type: Part Time, No Benefits (less than 20 hrs per week) Hours Per Week: 10 - 20 Additional Schedule Details: Fall 2026 Posted Salary Grade: Part Time Faculty/Students - 01 Retirement: None Contact Person: Dr. Nilesh Joshi Job Summary/Basic Functions The EKU Department of Engineering and Technology seeks an Institutional Work Study Student Lab Assistant, beginning Fall 2026, with options to renew as needed. This role primarily supports the department's laboratories, equipment and working spaces. Typical tasks can include assuring equipment is ready for student lab work, supporting lab maintenance, helping to create lab improvements, and assisting in the reconfiguring of our classroom and laboratory spaces. Student may also have opportunities to help prepare for department visitors (such as industry leaders) and/or to help with hosting events. Engineering and Technology majors are encouraged to apply. Minimum Qualifications Education: High School diploma or GED is required. Must be enrolled at EKU. Preferred Qualifications: Experience with Microsoft Office, Excel, and tools such as Google Docs is desired. Interest in learning about electrical and mechanical equipment and tools. Wants to be an effective contributor to our team and can exhibit strong problem-solving skills. Prepared to undertake different tasks and roles depending on department needs. Effective communication skills are helpful - meeting with visitors, preparing exhibits or demonstrations, etc. Job Duties: Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: Yes Special Instructions: Applicants should provide an official EKU email address and cell phone number for communication. Please submit a cover letter, resume, and contact information for 3 professional references. EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 62351f03 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 21R000 - Science, Tech, Engineering & Math 21R000 - Science, Tech, Engineering & Math Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) b086d73e Last Name (required) 38b5ff0a Email (required) e1726c1c Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graphic Design Studio Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 21R010 - College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sci The EKU School of Art and Design is seeking a dependable and organized student worker to assist with the day-to-day needs of the Graphic Design program. Student Assistant Richmond Campus