      "title": "Chemical Storage Student Laboratory Assistant",
      "description": "Chemical Storage Student Laboratory Assistant - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Home Why EKU Equal Opportunity & Title IX Benefits Contact Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Chemical Storage Student Laboratory Assistant 497699 Richmond Campus College of Science, Tech, Eng & Math Student Closing at: Sep 24 2026 - 23:55 EDT Add to favorites View favorites Title: Chemical Storage Student Laboratory Assistant Position Type: Student Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 21R000 - Science, Tech, Engineering & Math Division: 2R0000 - Academic Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver FLSA: Non-Exempt Schedule Type: Part Time, No Benefits (less than 20 hrs per week) Hours Per Week: 10 Additional Schedule Details: Shifts will vary on candidate’s availability during official office hours of Monday through Friday from 8:00 am to 4:30 pm. Posted Salary Grade: Students/Temporaries - 01 Retirement: None Contact Person: Mary Lamar Job Summary/Basic Functions The EKU College of Science, Technology, Engineering, and Mathematics is accepting applications for a Student Laboratory Assistant in the Chemical Storage Facility for the 2026-2027 Academic Year, starting August 2026, with option to renew, depending on shift availability and funding. Position pays $12/hour. Applicants must be enrolled at EKU and eligible for student employment. Responsibilities include but are not limited to the following: tracking and documentation of chemicals checked out to faculty, preparation of some solutions for laboratories, log-in of chemical waste generated by science labs, and assist with laboratory inspections. Applicants must have completed two semesters of first-year college chemistry with at least a grade of “C” or better. Chemistry and Forensic Science majors are encouraged to apply. Minimum Qualifications Education: Must be enrolled at EKU and eligible for student employment. Preferred Qualifications: Applicants must have completed two semesters of first-year college chemistry with at least a grade of “C” or better. They must also be enrolled at EKU and eligible for student employment. Job Duties: Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: Yes EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 59d7eede Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 21R000 - Science, Tech, Engineering & Math 21R000 - Science, Tech, Engineering & Math Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) 933a4533 Last Name (required) 8ba121f5 Email (required) 1fcd5704 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graphic Design Studio Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 21R010 - College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sci The EKU School of Art and Design is seeking a dependable and organized student worker to assist with the day-to-day needs of the Graphic Design program. Student Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 25R000 - Justice, Safety & Military Science Student Assistant will staff the College Advising Office front desk, where they wil