      "description": "Undergraduate Research Assistant - Biological Sciences - Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Home Why EKU Equal Opportunity & Title IX Benefits Contact Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Undergraduate Research Assistant - Biological Sciences 497702 Richmond Campus College of Health Sciences Student Closing at: Sep 10 2026 - 23:55 EDT Add to favorites View favorites Title: Undergraduate Research Assistant - Biological Sciences Position Type: Student Search Type: External - minimum 7 days Department: 21R000 - Science, Tech, Engineering & Math Division: 2R0000 - Academic Affairs Position Location: Richmond Campus Driver Classification: Non-Driver FLSA: Non-Exempt Hours Per Week: 10-20 hours per week Additional Schedule Details: Some nights and weekends may be required. Contact Person: Kendall.Simpson@eku.edu Job Summary/Basic Functions The Department of Biological Sciences is seeking a motivated and reliable undergraduate student researcher, starting Fall 2026. This position will work with a departmental faculty member involving hands-on laboratory tasks. The ideal candidate is detail-oriented, organized, and capable of working independently in a research-focused environment. Must be able to lift up to 50 lbs occasionally and carry up to 25 lbs. Prior lab experience is a plus but not required; training will be provided. This is an excellent opportunity for students interested in gaining practical experience in a research setting. Key Responsibilities: · Collecting and managing data · Maintaining accurate and efficient record keeping Qualifications: · Currently enrolled as an undergraduate student in a relevant scientific discipline · Responsible, punctual, and able to follow protocols precisely This position is 10 to 20 hours per week for the 2026-2027 academic year, renewable as needed. Flexible hours available during the academic year. Minimum Qualifications Education: Must be enrolled at EKU and be eligible for student employment. Preferred Qualifications: Must be enrolled at EKU and be eligible for student employment. Job Duties: Sponsorship: This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Funding Source: Institutional Open Until Filled: Yes Special Instructions: A cover letter and resume are required to apply. EEO Statement Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts or any employment policy or practice. Background Check Statement Offers of employment are contingent upon a satisfactory background check. Apply now! Sign up for job alerts! Job Alert 1eafcd19 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments 21R000 - Science, Tech, Engineering & Math 21R000 - Science, Tech, Engineering & Math Locations Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States First Name (required) 85ec63e2 Last Name (required) 978fc27b Email (required) c9d19758 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Graphic Design Studio Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 21R010 - College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sci The EKU School of Art and Design is seeking a dependable and organized student worker to assist with the day-to-day needs of the Graphic Design program. Student Assistant Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 25R000 - Justice, Safety & Military Science Student Assistant will staff the College Advising Office front desk, where they will schedule appointments for academic advisors, assist with basic advising questions, and direct visitors throughout the building.  Student Assistant will assist with direct recruitment initiatives, including but not limited to building tours, emails to prospective students, direct mail efforts, etc. Coordinator, Graduate Education Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 39R000 - Graduate Education & Research Admin Provides professional high level administrative support to graduate students, faculty, and staff by preparing reports, processing graduate student record requests, performing support functions such as preparing correspondence, receiving visitors, arranging conference calls and scheduling in-person meetings, creating, and sending communications, presenting to undergraduate and graduate student groups, and scheduling meetings. Will also train and provide technical direction to lower-level clerical staff. USAC Ambassador Education Abroad Student Worker Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 20R000 - Office of the Provost The Education Abroad Office is looking for an outgoing student worker with study abroad experience through USAC, who is interested in sharing their experience and supporting the office and other students in their efforts to study abroad. Specialist, Education & Career Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 77G010 - Student Affairs-Restricted Funds The Education and Career Specialist for the Appalachian Heartlands Talent Search  program at Eastern Kentucky University (EKU) provides academic, career, and financial guidance to help potential first-generation and income-eligible students successfully enter and complete postsecondary education. Associate Director, Educational Talent Search Richmond Campus, Kentucky, United States 77G010 - Student Affairs-Restricted Funds The Associate Director of Appalachian Heartlands Talent Search at Eastern Kentucky University (EKU) supports the program director in managing a federally funded TRIO project that helps middle school, high school, and adult learners from disadvantaged backgrounds pursue higher education. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 5c41f90b Last Name (required) 4d47a8dd Email (required) 0f08c9fa Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Equal Opportunity Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, and/or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts, or in any employment policy or practice. Any complaint arising by reason of alleged discrimination should be directed to the Office of Equal Opportunity & Title IX, Eastern Kentucky University, Jones Bldg. Room 416, Richmond, Kentucky 40475 (859) 622-8020 , or the Assistant Secretary for Civil Rights, U.S. Department of Education, Office for Civil Rights, Lyndon Baines Johnson Department of Education Building, 400 Maryland Avenue, SW, Washington, DC. 20202 1-800-421-3481(V) , 1-800-877-8339 (TTY) . Categories About Us | Contact Us | Contribute | Privacy Policy Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by Eastern Kentucky University . Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
