    "https://careers.eku.edu/jobs/search?page=2": {
      "title": "Search Page",
      "description": "Search Page Home Why EKU Equal Opportunity & Title IX Benefits Contact Applicant Login Kiosk mode Welcome to Eastern Kentucky University's Careers! At EKU, we are a school of opportunity. We create and sustain a workplace culture of excellence and high engagement, foster innovation, and growth, promote respect, and support the integration of the demands of work and life. Come join us in our mission! Skip to jobs search results Category Search categories 20 filter options found Category Academic Support Positions (4 items) 4 Administrative Support Positions (3 items) 3 Arlington (3 items) 3 Athletics Positions (10 items) 10 College of Business (8 items) 8 College of Education & Applied Human Sciences (3 items) 3 College of Health Sciences (5 items) 5 College of Justice, Safety & Military Science (15 items) 15 College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sciences (18 items) 18 College of Science, Tech, Eng & Math (20 items) 20 Financial Positions (3 items) 3 Hospitality Positions (2 items) 2 Maintenance Positions (1 items) 1 Management Positions (2 items) 2 Marketing Positions (1 items) 1 Model Lab School Positions (2 items) 2 Protective Services Positions (Police) (1 items) 1 Skilled Craft Positions (9 items) 9 Student Support Positions (81 items) 81 Technology Positions (2 items) 2 Employment Type Search employment types 9 filter options found Employment Type Fulltime Administrator (1 items) 1 Fulltime Faculty (9 items) 9 Fulltime Staff (38 items) 38 Graduate Assistant (4 items) 4 Model Staff & Faculty (2 items) 2 Part-Time Faculty (29 items) 29 Part-Time Staff (13 items) 13 Seasonal or Temporary (6 items) 6 Student (71 items) 71 City Search cities 3 filter options found City Other EKU Location (6 items) 6 Remote Opportunities (8 items) 8 Richmond Campus (156 items) 156 Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Student Worker 497701 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student This position operates within The Office of the Registrar and is an integral part of assisting with office duties. The student worker will help maintain accurate records, process various forms, and engage in projects that revolve around helping students. The start date will be at the beginning of the Fall 2026 semester. Applicants must be available to work during office hours 8 am - 4:30 pm Monday-Friday. Read more Cook, University Club 497662 Richmond Campus Hospitality Positions Fulltime Staff Being a country club cook involves working in the kitchen of a private country club, where members gather for leisure activities, social events, and sports. As a country club cook, your primary responsibility is to prepare and cook meals for club members, catering to their preferences and dietary requirements. Read more Supervisor, Grounds Zone 497616 Richmond Campus Skilled Craft Positions Fulltime Staff The Supervisor of Ground Zone is a working foreperson responsible for the completion of assigned grounds maintenance and operational tasks both individually and through direct reports and includes the performance of various tasks as required to maintain a high level of care inside the assigned zone. Read more Assistant, Electrician 497629 Richmond Campus Skilled Craft Positions Fulltime Staff The Electrician Assistant works directly with the electric shop supervisor on a daily basis and with the assistant director as need arises to assure that all university electrical systems operate at the highest efficiency. Read more Specialist, Grounds Zone 497617 Richmond Campus Skilled Craft Positions Fulltime Staff A Grounds Zone Specialist assists the Grounds Zone Foreperson in overseeing and ensuring completion of assigned grounds maintenance and operational tasks and includes performance of various tasks as required to maintain a high level of care inside assigned zone. Read more Interior Finisher II 497602 Richmond Campus Skilled Craft Positions Fulltime Staff An EKU Interior Finisher Tech II completes the initial construction and repairs of university floors, walls, and ceilings. An Interior Finisher Tech II will have knowledge and abilities to work with various finish materials such as ceramic, plaster, drywall, paint, caulk, VCT, LVT, carpet, etc. This position will work closely with the Craft Foreman and Structural Supervisor to complete work orders assigned in a quality, timely, and safe manner. Read more Student Worker Communications / Creative Content 497700 Richmond Campus Athletics Positions Student Support Positions Student Eastern Kentucky University Athletics is seeking a part-time Creative Assistant/Sports Information Director to support the athletic communications and creative content operations for EKU's intercollegiate athletics programs. Read more Analyst, Compliance Reporting 497578 Richmond Campus Administrative Support Positions Fulltime Staff The Systems Analyst, Compliance Reporting provides technical and analytical support to ensure the accuracy, integrity, and compliance of student enrollment and graduation data reported by the Office of the Registrar. The incumbent serves as the primary administrator for National Student Clearinghouse (NSCH) enrollment and degree reporting, ensuring timely and accurate submissions in accordance with federal, state, and institutional reporting requirements.\n \nThis position serves as a liaison between the Registrar's Office and IT on matters related to compliance reporting, Banner Student System functionality, and reporting enhancements. The Systems Analyst examines student data, investigates reporting discrepancies, coordinates system testing, and develops processes to enhance data quality, reporting accuracy, and operational efficiency. The position also provides secondary functional support for Degree Works and the Degrees Team by assisting with degree audit reviews, approved academic exceptions, audit-related inquiries, and the resolution of student record and degree audit issues. Read more Coordinator, Housing Assignments & Operations 497695 Richmond Campus Administrative Support Positions Student Support Positions Fulltime Staff The Coordinator, Housing Assignments & Operations is responsible for coordinating the University's housing assignment processes and supporting the effective management of residential occupancy. This position oversees critical administrative functions including room assignments, billing, room changes, contract exemptions, accommodations, and re-contracting. Serves as the operational bridge between administrative systems, and front-facing student communications. Read more Admissions Counselor 497669 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Fulltime Staff This Admissions Counselor position is responsible for recruiting qualified undergraduate in-of-state and out-state students to the University by developing and implementing data-driven strategies, conducting market analysis, and using predictive modeling to guide outreach. This role serves as a primary liaison to school counselors and community organizations while building strong relationships with prospective students and their families throughout the college search process. The counselor manages an assigned territory through a Client Relationship Management (CRM) system, ensuring consistent follow-up with inquiries, applicants, and admitted students. Communication takes place across multiple platforms, including phone, email, written correspondence, social media, and presentations. The position also involves traveling to college fairs at the state, regional, and national levels, visiting high schools in designated markets, and participating in University-hosted recruitment events. Read more Card Services Associate 497694 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Colonel Card Services is the first face-to-face interaction many patrons have with the university. A Card Services Associate will deliver exceptional front-line customer service to a diverse client base, including students, faculty, administrators, and university contractors. Read more Game Operations Staff (PL)-Broadcasting Only 497693 Richmond Campus Athletics Positions Part-Time Staff Game operations staff broadcasting will assist in setting up and breaking down all cameras before and after home events. The crew will assist the director and assistant director in streaming games/matches online through ESPNPlus. The staff will also be responsible for operating a camera during streams. Read more FSE Student Ashland Fire Lab Technician 497691 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student The Fire and Safety Engineering Technology program is now hiring student workers for the Fire Protection Labs at the Ashland Building to aid the faculty and Lab Coordinator in the development, construction, execution and recycling of various fire-based lab activities. Active mentorship will teach you many valuable hands-on skills. This job features indoor and outdoor work, some moderate lifting, and the use of various hand and power tools. This position is for Fall 2026 and Spring/Summer 2027 semesters. Read more Special Collections and Archives Library Student Assistant 497689 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Students in this position are expected to be able to work independently with little supervision. They must be detail oriented, able to follow instructions, and maintain confidentiality. A work schedule is typically ten hours a week between 9 a.m.-5 p.m., Monday through Friday. Read more College of Health Sciences Student Learning Assistant 497685 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student The Center for Retention, Progression, and Graduation in the College of Health Sciences at Eastern Kentucky University seeks to hire learning assistants. Read more Registered Nurse PRN 497686 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Part-Time Staff Registered nurse who performs competent and compassionate care to patients using nursing skills, assessment and education based on knowledge of the nursing process Read more Student Enforcement Officer 497582 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Student Parking Enforcement Officer Read more Assistant Chief Flight Instructor 497674 Richmond Campus College of Justice, Safety & Military Science Fulltime Staff The Assistant Chief Flight Instructor assists in overseeing Private, Instrument, Commercial, Multi Engine, CFI/CFII/MEI certificates and ratings in the collegiate Part 141 program. The Assistant Chief Flight Instructor assists in the administration and oversight of flight operation and flight course portions of the aviation program. The incumbent must possess and maintain a strong working knowledge of all applicable Federal Aviation Regulations (FARs) for Part 141, and will assist with all FAA related paperwork and documentation. Read more Model Lab School Archery Assistant Coach 497650 Richmond Campus Model Lab School Positions Seasonal or Temporary Be a part of a winning archery team in a world-class school environment as the Assistant Coach at Model Laboratory School. The Patriots have a rich heritage and a family atmosphere where teamwork is valued. Read more Student Work Study for Archaeological Work 497682 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student EKU Anthropology Programs is seeking a dedicated, responsible Student Laboratory Technician to assist in the archaeology laboratory to catalog, identify, analyze, curate, etc. artifacts and samples from the field schools and other EKU projects. Duties include general office support (email correspondence, filing, data entry, use of complex office equipment, light cleaning), and other duties as assigned. Review of candidates will occur as needed and continue until position is filled. Read more Part Time Online Facilitator - Computer Science & Information Technology 497673 Richmond Campus College of Science, Tech, Eng & Math Part-Time Faculty The Dept of Computer Science & Information Technology seeks part-time online Facilitator positions, beginning August 2026, with options to renew on a semester-to-semester basis. Part-time facilitators support Faculty Instructors of Record with undergraduate instruction in online courses - up to 9 credit hours per semester. Bachelor's degree in CIS, MIS, Informatics, or a closely related field; or a Bachelor's degree plus at least 18 graduate credit hours in CIS, MIS, Informatics, or a closely related field. Read more Music Events Assistant 497678 Richmond Campus College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sciences Student Support Positions Student The School of Music is seeking a student to help with departmental duties for SoM events. Read more ICCA Office Assistant 497679 Richmond Campus College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sciences Student Support Positions Student Institute for Creative & Collaborative Arts is seeking a student to help with departmental duties. Read more Student Worker - Model Laboratory Early Childhood Development Center 2026-27 School Year 497677 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Model Staff & Faculty Student Enrich your life as a student worker at Model Lab School's Early Childhood Development Center engaging with preschool students during the 2026-27 school year! Read more Development and Alumni Engagement Student Liaison 497676 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student The Development and Alumni Engagement Student Liaison will carry out daily administrative duties of the division, provide customer service to alumni, donors, students, and potential future colonels, and work closely with the Development and Alumni Engagement team as well as the Student Alumni Ambassador Advisor's to plan, organize, promote, execute, and follow-up all alumni and philanthropic events. Read more Graduate Assistant - Construction Management Program 497672 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Graduate Assistant The Graduate Assistant within the Construction Management Program is an enrolled EKU student in the Graduate degree program that will work with the Faculty and Staff to perform required duties as needed on a daily basis regarding classes and office tasks. Read more Student Involvement Associate 497675 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Student Employees assist with the daily operations of the Center for Student Involvement (CSI) by providing excellent customer service, supporting campus events and programs, and contributing to a welcoming and engaging environment for students, staff, and visitors. Read more Housing Student Technician 497671 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student The Student Housing Technician will work as part of a team to make basic repairs and perform maintenance in our campus residence halls. Read more Colonel Creator & Engagement Ambassador 497659 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student This role offers the opportunity to represent the Eastern Kentucky University brand across the University’s main social media platforms, create engaging content and serve as a student voice for current and prospective students in EKU's department of Marketing and Communications. Read more Clinical Skills Lab Worker 497667 Richmond Campus College of Health Sciences Student Support Positions Student Working in nursing skills lab to set up and break down for nursing classes and simulation. Read more Displaying 31 - 60 of 170 in total ‹ 1 2 3 4 5 6 › Equal Opportunity Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, and/or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts, or in any employment policy or practice. Any complaint arising by reason of alleged discrimination should be directed to the Office of Equal Opportunity & Title IX, Eastern Kentucky University, Jones Bldg. Room 416, Richmond, Kentucky 40475 (859) 622-8020 , or the Assistant Secretary for Civil Rights, U.S. Department of Education, Office for Civil Rights, Lyndon Baines Johnson Department of Education Building, 400 Maryland Avenue, SW, Washington, DC. 20202 1-800-421-3481(V) , 1-800-877-8339 (TTY) . Categories About Us | Contact Us | Contribute | Privacy Policy Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by Eastern Kentucky University . Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept"
