      "title": "Search Page",
      "description": "Search Page Home Why EKU Equal Opportunity & Title IX Benefits Contact Applicant Login Kiosk mode Welcome to Eastern Kentucky University's Careers! At EKU, we are a school of opportunity. We create and sustain a workplace culture of excellence and high engagement, foster innovation, and growth, promote respect, and support the integration of the demands of work and life. Come join us in our mission! Skip to jobs search results Category Search categories 20 filter options found Category Academic Support Positions (4 items) 4 Administrative Support Positions (3 items) 3 Arlington (3 items) 3 Athletics Positions (10 items) 10 College of Business (8 items) 8 College of Education & Applied Human Sciences (3 items) 3 College of Health Sciences (5 items) 5 College of Justice, Safety & Military Science (15 items) 15 College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sciences (18 items) 18 College of Science, Tech, Eng & Math (20 items) 20 Financial Positions (3 items) 3 Hospitality Positions (2 items) 2 Maintenance Positions (1 items) 1 Management Positions (2 items) 2 Marketing Positions (1 items) 1 Model Lab School Positions (2 items) 2 Protective Services Positions (Police) (1 items) 1 Skilled Craft Positions (9 items) 9 Student Support Positions (81 items) 81 Technology Positions (2 items) 2 Employment Type Search employment types 9 filter options found Employment Type Fulltime Administrator (1 items) 1 Fulltime Faculty (9 items) 9 Fulltime Staff (38 items) 38 Graduate Assistant (4 items) 4 Model Staff & Faculty (2 items) 2 Part-Time Faculty (29 items) 29 Part-Time Staff (13 items) 13 Seasonal or Temporary (6 items) 6 Student (71 items) 71 City Search cities 3 filter options found City Other EKU Location (6 items) 6 Remote Opportunities (8 items) 8 Richmond Campus (156 items) 156 Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Departmental Office Student Worker 497666 Richmond Campus College of Justice, Safety & Military Science Student Support Positions Student Responsible student workers needed for the School of Justice Studies. Read more CFOR Office Assistant 497664 Richmond Campus College of Science, Tech, Eng & Math Student The Department of Chemistry and Forensic Science is accepting applications for a Student Office Assistant. The employee will direct and provide front office customer service, faculty support, assist with general office duties such as data entries, filing, maintaining office supply inventory, posting announcements, assist with special events, etc. Appointment is for the Fall 2026 semester, with the option to renew as openings are available. Read more Environmental Health and Safety Technician 497663 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student EH&S Technicians will participate in the Department of Environmental Health and Safety activities including AED inspections, life safety building inspections, laboratory safety inspections, fume hood testing, hazardous chemical inventories, hazardous waste tracking, safety training (OSHA), environmental training (EPA). Read more ASL & ITP Student Worker 497655 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student The ASL and Interpreter Education programs are seeking a qualified ASL tutor. Read more Fire Extinguisher Lab Technician 497661 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student The fire extinguisher lab at Eastern Kentucky University is seeking students to conduct fire extinguisher inspections and maintenance of fire extinguishers on campus. Read more CFOR Lab Prep Assistant 497658 Richmond Campus College of Science, Tech, Eng & Math Student The Department of Chemistry and Forensic Science is accepting applications for Lab Prep Assistant(s). Appointment is for the Fall 2026 semester, with the option to renew as openings are available. Read more Part-Time Faculty - Mathematics & Statistics 497653 Richmond Campus College of Science, Tech, Eng & Math Part-Time Faculty The Department of Mathematics and Statistics at Eastern Kentucky University invites applications for a part-time faculty position to teach courses in the Academic Year 2026-2027. Applicants should hold an earned master’s degree in mathematics, or a related field with at least 18 credit hours in graduate-level mathematics, from a regionally (SACS, Middle States, North Central, etc.) accredited or internationally recognized institution at the time of appointment. Part-time faculty may teach up to nine credit hours, depending on departmental needs. Read more Bratzke Center- Student Tutor 497654 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student This is a position for current students who are passionate about tutoring student-athletes in various courses offered at EKU. Students employed in this position are responsible for ensuring the ongoing success of the program by serving as a learning resource for our student athletes and representing the Bratzke Center in a professional manner.\n\nMust provide at least 2 academic references to be contacted to be considered (professor, academic advisor, mentor, current/past EKU supervisor if have worked on campus etc..) Read more Assistant Professor, Special Education 497217 Richmond Campus College of Education & Applied Human Sciences Fulltime Faculty The School of Education at Eastern Kentucky University invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor for Academic Year 2026-2027. Applicants should hold an earned Ph.D. in Special Education or a related field from an accredited institution at the time of appointment. ABD applicants may be considered with evidence of a scheduled doctoral defense that occurs no later than May prior to a Fall appointment. The position begins August 2026. Read more Assistant Professor of Counselor Education 497305 Richmond Campus College of Education & Applied Human Sciences Fulltime Faculty The CACREP-accredited Counselor Education Program in the Department of Clinical Therapeutic Programs at Eastern Kentucky University invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor for Academic Year 2026-2027. Applicants should hold an earned Ed.D. or Ph.D. in Counselor Education and Supervision from a CACREP-accredited institution/program. ABD applicants may be considered with evidence of a scheduled doctoral defense that occurs no later than May 2026 prior to an August 2026 appointment. Applicants must also hold an active state counseling license and both be eligible for Kentucky clinical counseling licensure and willing to pursue Kentucky licensure within one year. The position begins August 2026. Read more Part-Time Secondary Instructors - Biological Sciences 497643 Richmond Campus College of Science, Tech, Eng & Math Part-Time Faculty The Dept Biological Sciences at EKU is seeking part-time Secondary Instructors starting Fall 2026 to work with program faculty assisting in teaching undergraduate lectures & laboratories.  Required: Bachelor’s degree in the teaching (or related) discipline, or Bachelor's degree with at least 18 graduate hours in the teaching (or related) discipline. Read more Part-time Faculty, Dept. of Agriculture 497560 Richmond Campus College of Science, Tech, Eng & Math Student Support Positions Part-Time Faculty The Department of Agriculture at EKU is seeking part-time instructors to teach undergraduate lectures and laboratories, starting Fall 2026 semester with options to renew. Candidates must have a minimum of a Master's degree with at least 18 graduate credit hours in the related field  from a regionally (SACS, Middle States, North Central, etc.) accredited or internationally recognized institution; Ph.D. preferred. Read more Part-Time Faculty, OSH 497652 Richmond Campus College of Justice, Safety & Military Science Part-Time Faculty The University is accepting applications for Part-Time Faculty in our Occupational Safety (OSH) program on campus on an ongoing and as-needed basis.\nWhen an opening is available, your application will be considered in the applicant pool. Read more CFOR Undergraduate Lab Assistant 497645 Richmond Campus College of Science, Tech, Eng & Math Student The Department of Chemistry and Forensic Science is seeking Undergraduate Laboratory Assistants to assist with the coverage of laboratory courses under the supervision of the laboratory course coordinator and/or a faculty supervisor. Read more Coordinator, Hospitality Services 497633 Richmond Campus Arlington Hospitality Positions Fulltime Staff The Hospitality Services Coordinator supports the Hospitality Operations Manager in delivering exceptional service and daily operations at the University Club at Arlington. This position is responsible for overseeing the execution of club events, supervising seasonal pool operations, and ensuring an outstanding experience for members, guests, alumni, donors, and university partners. Read more Director of Operations 497634 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Fulltime Administrator The Director of Housing Operations is responsible for the strategic planning, implementation, and evaluation of a comprehensive university housing operation, with a primary focus on driving business innovation through data systems and . The incumbent provides leadership for developing responsible, effective, and ethical business practices while overseeing the daily operation of the operations portion of the housing portfolio. The Director of Operations works closely with the Director of Residence Life to ensure all efforts of Housing & Residence Life are cohesive and efficient. Actively serving as the leader of administration, facilities, and technology for the department, the Director spearheads innovation across all housing operational functions. This role leads facilitation and liaises with campus partners on advanced systems configurations, workflow automations, and integrations. Creating data-driven assessments and reports, the Director works to optimize occupancy, streamline central office processes, and inform institutional decision-making. Read more Coordinator, Fraternity & Sorority Life and Student Involvement 497632 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Fulltime Staff Coordinates and supports the administration of Fraternity & Sorority Life and Student Involvement by advising student leaders, facilitating organizational operations, promoting student engagement, ensuring compliance with university policies, and collaborating with campus partners to enhance the student experience. Read more Aquatic Ecology Research Assistant 497648 Richmond Campus College of Science, Tech, Eng & Math Student Support Positions Student The Department of Biological Sciences is seeking a motivated and reliable undergraduate student researcher to assist with aquatic biology research. Read more Natural Areas Intern 497649 Richmond Campus College of Science, Tech, Eng & Math Student Natural Areas student employees function to support land stewardship activities, community outreach and other responsibilities associated with our mission. Read more Associate/Senior Associate Athletics Director of Development 497608 Richmond Campus Administrative Support Positions Fulltime Staff The Associate/Senior Associate Athletics Director of Development will be an integral part of the Development and Alumni Engagement team and will also serve as a member of the Athletics Department senior staff. \n\nThis position will work closely with the Vice President & Director of Athletics to align development efforts with the broader vision and priorities of EKU Athletics. Under the supervision of the Assistant Vice President for Major Gifts, this position will:\n\n●\tCultivate, solicit, secure, and steward major gifts ($25,000 and greater).\n●\tExecute a minimum of 12 substantial face-to-face visits per month and a combination of annual and major proposal goals based on portfolio value and tenure.\n●\tActively engage a prospect portfolio of 80+ individuals/households, working with the Development team, coaches, athletics staff and other campus leaders on unique donor strategies.\n●\tTravel frequently for prospect visits and athletic events, including a minimum of one out of state trip per month.\n●\tBe responsible for recruiting members to the Colonel Club with leadership annual gifts ($1,000 - $5,000).\n●\tAssist with coordination of hospitality areas.\n●\tResponsible for logging metric and contact information into the University system.\n●\tMotivates administrators and coaches to participate in the development process and solicitation of gifts.\n●\tOversee specific giving initiatives, events, and projects with the purpose of donor acquisition, portfolio building, and donor participation.\n●\tAttend a high number of EKU Athletics games and events, including nights and weekends. Read more Student - HVAC Support Technician (Entry Level) 497642 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Assist with daily HVAC and control system repairs and service work Read more Musical Theatre Production Team Member Fall 2026 497640 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Seasonal or Temporary EKU Musical Theatre Program is hiring a Production Team Member that will act as assistant in choreography and directing for the fall 2026 production of \"Young Frankenstein.\" Read more Part-Time Faculty, Economics and Finance 497641 Richmond Campus College of Business Part-Time Faculty The College of Business at Eastern Kentucky University invites applications for a part-time faculty position to teach courses in economics and finance. Read more Graduate Assistant 497639 Richmond Campus College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sciences Student Support Positions Graduate Assistant GA for Dep't of Government Read more Student Worker 497637 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Will work in various roles as needed for the School of Applied Human Sciences. Duties can include assisting in food labs and office work. Read more Part-Time Faculty, Sociology 497636 Richmond Campus College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sciences Part-Time Faculty The Sociology Part-Time Instructor will lead or facilitate instruction for Sociology courses such as SOC 131 Introductory Sociology, SOC 245 Sociology of the Family, SOC 310 Population and Society, SOC 365 Social Change in Appalachia, SOC 380 Jobs and Professionalization, SOC 300 Animals and Society, SOC 383 Environment and Society, and SOC 399 Gender & Society. Read more Student Office Assistant - Mathematics and Statistics 497627 Richmond Campus College of Science, Tech, Eng & Math Student The Department of Mathematics and Statistics is accepting applications for a Student Office Assistant for the Fall 2026 semester.  The assistant will provide support with general office duties such as copying, filing, mailings, monitoring supply inventory, and running errands as needed.  Applicants should have working knowledge of Microsoft office programs, time management skills, and be detail oriented. Read more Accounting Specialist 497590 Richmond Campus Financial Positions Fulltime Staff A University Accounting Specialist is responsible for timely and accurate analysis, reconciliation updating, and reporting of university information. This information is provided to both internal and external entities. The incumbent also provides technical direction, consultation and customer service to a variety of constituents. Incumbent will work in the Accounting Office. Read more Assistant Director, Sports Medicine Football 497593 Richmond Campus Athletics Positions Fulltime Staff The Assistant Director of Football Sports Medicine is responsible for the prevention, treatment, and rehabilitation of athletic injuries to collegiate athletes. In addition, this position administers drug testing, insurance coordination, and travels with athletic teams to all events. The incumbent reports to the Assistant Athletic Director for Sports Medicine in the administration of a Division I intercollegiate Athletic program in adherence to all university and Kentucky Board of Medical Licensure regulations. Read more Associate Director, Instructional Design Center 497575 Remote Opportunities Academic Support Positions Fulltime Staff The Associate Director of the Instructional Design Center supports the design, delivery, and continuous improvement of learning experiences across EKU. This position provides leadership, coordination, and support for instructional design, educational technology, faculty partnerships, and unit operations, with a focus on usability, innovation, and student success. Read more Displaying 61 - 90 of 170 in total ‹ 1 2 3 4 5 6 › Equal Opportunity Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, and/or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts, or in any employment policy or practice. Any complaint arising by reason of alleged discrimination should be directed to the Office of Equal Opportunity & Title IX, Eastern Kentucky University, Jones Bldg. Room 416, Richmond, Kentucky 40475 (859) 622-8020 , or the Assistant Secretary for Civil Rights, U.S. Department of Education, Office for Civil Rights, Lyndon Baines Johnson Department of Education Building, 400 Maryland Avenue, SW, Washington, DC. 20202 1-800-421-3481(V) , 1-800-877-8339 (TTY) . Categories About Us | Contact Us | Contribute | Privacy Policy Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by Eastern Kentucky University . Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept"
