      "description": "Search Page Home Why EKU Equal Opportunity & Title IX Benefits Contact Applicant Login Kiosk mode Welcome to Eastern Kentucky University's Careers! At EKU, we are a school of opportunity. We create and sustain a workplace culture of excellence and high engagement, foster innovation, and growth, promote respect, and support the integration of the demands of work and life. Come join us in our mission! Skip to jobs search results Category Search categories 20 filter options found Category Academic Support Positions (4 items) 4 Administrative Support Positions (3 items) 3 Arlington (3 items) 3 Athletics Positions (10 items) 10 College of Business (8 items) 8 College of Education & Applied Human Sciences (3 items) 3 College of Health Sciences (5 items) 5 College of Justice, Safety & Military Science (15 items) 15 College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sciences (18 items) 18 College of Science, Tech, Eng & Math (20 items) 20 Financial Positions (3 items) 3 Hospitality Positions (2 items) 2 Maintenance Positions (1 items) 1 Management Positions (2 items) 2 Marketing Positions (1 items) 1 Model Lab School Positions (2 items) 2 Protective Services Positions (Police) (1 items) 1 Skilled Craft Positions (9 items) 9 Student Support Positions (81 items) 81 Technology Positions (2 items) 2 Employment Type Search employment types 9 filter options found Employment Type Fulltime Administrator (1 items) 1 Fulltime Faculty (9 items) 9 Fulltime Staff (38 items) 38 Graduate Assistant (4 items) 4 Model Staff & Faculty (2 items) 2 Part-Time Faculty (29 items) 29 Part-Time Staff (13 items) 13 Seasonal or Temporary (6 items) 6 Student (71 items) 71 City Search cities 3 filter options found City Other EKU Location (6 items) 6 Remote Opportunities (8 items) 8 Richmond Campus (156 items) 156 Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Staff Psychologist 497259 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Fulltime Staff An EKU Staff Psychologist assists in the mission of the Counseling Center by promoting personal, social, and career development of EKU students. A Staff Psychologist provides the full range of counseling center services: individual and group counseling, assessment, career counseling, , outreach, education/training of the university community on early detection of distressed students and how to refer, crisis intervention, consultation, referral, supervision, and outcome research. Providing the standard of care services and adhering to professional standards is highly emphasized, including the maintenance of appropriate clinical documentation according to established protocol. Utilizes relevant assessment/diagnostic tools for identification of needs of client. Rotates coverage of after-hours on-call phone. Other duties as assigned by the Director.\n\nSalary for this position is $75,000.00 Read more Game Operations Staff (PL) 497626 Richmond Campus Athletics Positions Part-Time Staff Game operations staff will be responsible for aiding in all aspects of game day operations for the EKU Athletic Department. This includes but is not limited to game & event setup, ticketing, statistics, first aid, parking, and table crew duties responsibilities. Read more Aviation Student Worker- Flight Line Attendant 497624 Other EKU Location Student Support Positions Student EKU's Fixed Based Operation (FBO) at the Madison Airport located in Richmond/Berea is looking for a Flight Line Attendant. Read more Athletics Facilities & Operations Lead (Part-Time Staff) 497625 Richmond Campus Athletics Positions Part-Time Staff The Athletics Facilities & Operations Lead plays a critical role in supporting and executing the day-to-day functions of athletic facility operations and game/event management. Read more Student Financial Aid Admin 497622 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student The Student Financial Aid department is currently seeking student employee(s) who will provide excellent and detailed administrative clerical support.  The student worker(s) duties will involve scanning, indexing, checking mail, running errands on campus, clerical support and other assigned duties.  We are seeking students who are available to work 15-20 hours per week Monday through Friday between the hours of 8am to 4:30pm. Read more America Reads Tutor 497621 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student The student employee will work with elementary-aged children grades K-5 under the direct supervision of a classroom teacher. Read more Center for Student Parents, Program Participant 497619 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Center for Student Parents Program Participant will participate in academic advising, career counseling, work readiness, employment training, and other activities related to retention, graduation, and employment. \n\nApplicant must receive KTAP benefits or in the process of receiving KTAP benefits to be eligible for this position. Read more Student Associate - Equal Opportunity & Title IX 497607 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student The Student Associate supports the Office of Equal Opportunity & Title IX through administrative support, campus outreach, educational programming, and office operations. This position offers students the opportunity to develop professional skills while contributing to the University's commitment to equal opportunity and a respectful campus environment. Read more Eastern Progress Editor 497606 Richmond Campus College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sciences Student Eastern Progress editors oversee content creation for easternprogress.com and creation of the Eastern Progress magazine. Editors are responsible for writing stories, producing photo, video and audio products, and mentoring journalism peers. Read more Part-Time Faculty, Philosophy 497605 Richmond Campus College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sciences Part-Time Faculty The Department of History, Philosophy, and Religious Studies invites applications for a part-time faculty position to teach introductory courses in Philosophy and Ethics in-person and online. Read more Bilingual Peer Academic Coach (PL) (GA/Student) 497598 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Peer-to-peer support through a tailored student academic coaching approach that builds on tutoring and mentoring in a relationship rich environment for academic engagement and success. \n\nStudent-workers will help organize study sessions, maintain the space, tutor based on their majors and skills, and mentor students with time-management, study habits, and social practices for academic engagement. Positions might also include tutoring language students and students that might not be in your college. This is a Student Employee position for 3-20 hours per week and may start at $12.00 per hour. This position will require you to work with students reviewing target language, academic subjects, and specific course assignments. May also include support time assisting faculty and staff with recruitment, retention, and community outreach. Computer knowledge is helpful as well as familiarity with office equipment. Read more Bilingual Peer Academic Coach (PL) (GA/Student) 497599 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Peer-to-peer support through a tailored student academic coaching approach that builds on tutoring and mentoring in a relationship rich environment for academic engagement and success. \n\nStudent-workers will help organize study sessions, maintain the space, tutor based on their majors and skills, and mentor students with time-management, study habits, and social practices for academic engagement. Positions might also include tutoring language students and students that might not be in your college. This is a Student Employee position for 3-20 hours per week and may start at $12.00 per hour. This position will require you to work with students reviewing target language, academic subjects, and specific course assignments. May also include support time assisting faculty and staff with recruitment, retention, and community outreach. Computer knowledge is helpful as well as familiarity with office equipment. Read more Part-Time Faculty, Dept. of Social Work 497595 Richmond Campus College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sciences Student Support Positions Part-Time Faculty The Department of Social Work at Eastern Kentucky University invites applications for a part-time faculty position to teach online and in person courses in the BSW  and MSW programs. Courses may include, but are not limited to:\nIntroduction to Social Work; Social Work Policy; Human Behavior in the Social Environment and Social Work Practice. Read more Library Student Assistant 497585 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student The library is seeking motivated and reliable Federal Work Study-eligible students committed to our mission of serving the EKU community. Read more Powell Welcome Desk - Student Employee 497580 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student The Office of Student Affairs is seeking a student with front-desk experience and interpersonal, hospitality-based skills for the Powell Welcome Desk. Read more CFOR Tutor 497581 Richmond Campus College of Science, Tech, Eng & Math Student The Department of Chemistry and Forensic Science is accepting applications for a CFOR Tutor. Appointment is for the Fall 2026 semester, with option to renew as openings are available. Read more Coordinator, Fitness Programs 497571 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Fulltime Staff The Coordinator of Fitness will provide strategic oversight, creative support, and supervision to the department’s efforts toward encouraging holistic wellbeing. This position is designed to promote the benefits of movement and exercise, and to provide programming designed to enable the campus community to pursue movement in a variety of fitness modalities. This is done successfully by demonstrating the department’s values through inviting and engaging recreational opportunities that are targeted toward students primarily and the campus/public secondarily. Read more Athletic Trainer, Sports Medicine 497574 Richmond Campus Athletics Positions Fulltime Staff This position is responsible for the prevention, treatment, and rehabilitation of athletic injuries to collegiate athletes.  In addition, the Athletic Trainer for Sports Medicine administers drug testing, insurance coordination, and travels with athletic teams to all events. The incumbent reports to the Associate Athletic Director of Sports Medicine in the administration of a Division I intercollegiate Athletic program in adherence to all university and Kentucky Board of Medical Licensure regulations. Read more Student Employee, Recycle & Waste Management 497577 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Student employee that assists the facilities team with campus recycling. Read more Employee Wellness Graduate Assistant 497576 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Graduate Assistant Graduate Assistant for EKU Employee Wellness and Benefits office. Read more Information Security Engineer 497283 Richmond Campus Technology Positions Fulltime Staff An Eastern Kentucky University Information Security Engineer is responsible for designing, implementing, and maintaining technical security controls that protect university information systems and data. This role combines hands-on security engineering and operational responsibilities with governance, risk, and compliance (GRC) support to ensure security controls are effectively implemented, monitored, documented, and aligned with institutional policies, legal requirements, and industry best practices. Read more Director, Military & Veteran Affairs 497563 Richmond Campus Management Positions Student Support Positions Fulltime Staff The Director implements, facilitates and manages a coordinated plan for recruitment, enrollment, retention and matriculation of veteran and military students, both resident and online, while ensuring program success and federal and state regulatory compliance. The incumbent plays an integral role in coordinating campus-wide training and development on issues related to the veteran and military student population. Read more Music Graduate Assistant 497567 Richmond Campus College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sciences Student Support Positions Graduate Assistant Assist the faculty in the School of Music in ensemble support. Read more Collaborative Pianist 497568 Richmond Campus College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sciences Seasonal or Temporary Seeking a collaborative pianist for vocal and instrumental performances. Read more Intramural Sports Official 497565 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Campus Recreation is accepting applications for Intramural Sport Officials. Read more Theatre Student Employee - Fall 2026 497564 Richmond Campus College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sciences Student Support Positions Student Federal Work Study Student hire for the Musical Theatre Program for positions anywhere from scenic painter, to office worker, to costuming assistant, and more. Read more Part-Time Faculty, Aviation 497562 Richmond Campus College of Justice, Safety & Military Science Part-Time Faculty Teaches part-time for the Aviation program at Eastern Kentucky University.  Primary responsibility is to teach courses related to the Aviation discipline such as, but not limited to, Aviation Law, UAS, Management/Leadership, Human Factors/Safety, and Professional Flight. Read more Part-Time Faculty, Communication Sciences and Disorders 497561 Richmond Campus College of Education & Applied Human Sciences Student Support Positions Part-Time Faculty The Department of Clinical Therapeutic Programs is accepting applications for part time adjuncts on a regular basis. Applications will be reviewed on an as needed basis as positions become available. Read more Part-Time Online Facilitator 497559 Remote Opportunities College of Health Sciences Part-Time Faculty Online part-time facilitator for RN-BSN, MSN (FNP or PMHNP) or DNP programs. Read more Big E Central Sr. Peer Counselor 497556 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Big E Central (BEC) Sr. Peer Counselor Read more Displaying 91 - 120 of 170 in total ‹ 1 2 3 4 5 6 › Equal Opportunity Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, and/or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts, or in any employment policy or practice. Any complaint arising by reason of alleged discrimination should be directed to the Office of Equal Opportunity & Title IX, Eastern Kentucky University, Jones Bldg. Room 416, Richmond, Kentucky 40475 (859) 622-8020 , or the Assistant Secretary for Civil Rights, U.S. Department of Education, Office for Civil Rights, Lyndon Baines Johnson Department of Education Building, 400 Maryland Avenue, SW, Washington, DC. 20202 1-800-421-3481(V) , 1-800-877-8339 (TTY) . Categories About Us | Contact Us | Contribute | Privacy Policy Copyright © 2026 All Rights Reserved by Eastern Kentucky University . Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept"
