more Admissions Recruitment Ambassador 497554 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student The Admissions Recruitment Ambassadors (ARA) play a vital role in shaping the visit experience at Eastern Kentucky University. As key representatives of the Office of Enrollment Management, ARAs assist in providing prospective students, families, and guests with a welcoming and positive atmosphere during their visit to the university. Their responsibilities include engaging with visitors, offering information, and ensuring that all guests have an informative and enjoyable experience. The ARA role demands individuals who are reliable, detail-oriented, and eager to interact with the public, helping to enhance the university's recruitment efforts. Read more E-Presence Facilitator 497553 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student EKU is seeking an E-Presence Facilitator for Fall 2026 on the Richmond campus. Read more Athletics Facilities & Operations Lead (Part-Time Staff) 497552 Richmond Campus Athletics Positions Part-Time Staff The Athletics Facilities & Operations Lead plays a critical role in supporting and executing the day-to-day functions of athletic facility operations and game/event management. Read more Visiting Lecturer (Biomedical Sciences) 497523 Richmond Campus College of Science, Tech, Eng & Math Fulltime Faculty The Department of Biological Sciences at Eastern Kentucky University invites applications for a 9-month Visiting Lecturer for Academic Year 2026-2027. Applicants should hold an earned Ph.D. in Biology (anatomy and physiology) or a related field from an accredited institution at the time of appointment. Review of applications will begin 30 June 2026. The position begins 1 August 2026. This position is not eligible for visa sponsorship. Read more Part-Time Faculty Clinical Instructor 497547 Richmond Campus College of Health Sciences Part-Time Faculty Undergraduate clinical instructor for AASN or BSN programs Read more Student Employee: EKU Center for the Arts 497546 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Our team is looking for friendly faces and flexible schedules! Read more Arlington Groundskeeper 497501 Other EKU Location Arlington Seasonal or Temporary As a groundskeeper at University Club at Arlington, your main responsibility will be to ensure that the golf course and surrounding grounds are well maintained and attractive for club members and visitors alike. Read more Part-Time Faculty, Business Law 497544 Richmond Campus College of Business Part-Time Faculty The College of Business at Eastern Kentucky University invites applications for a part-time faculty position to teach courses in business law. Read more Student Employee 497543 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Student Student Accounting Services is seeking to hire a student employee to provide office support. Read more Part-Time Faculty, School of Music 497287 Richmond Campus College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sciences Part-Time Faculty The School of Music at Eastern Kentucky University invites applications for a part-time faculty position to teach courses in Music. Read more Assistant Professor of Management 497527 Richmond Campus College of Business Fulltime Faculty The College of Business at Eastern Kentucky University in Richmond, Kentucky invites applications for a tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant Professor for Academic Year 2027-28. Applicants should hold an earned Ph.D. or D.B.A in Management, with a specific teaching and research focus in Entrepreneurship, from an AACSB International accredited institution at the time of appointment. ABD applicants may be considered with evidence of a scheduled doctoral defense that occurs no later than May prior to a Fall appointment. The position begins August 2027. Read more Athletic Trainer, Sports Medicine 497526 Richmond Campus Athletics Positions Fulltime Staff This position is responsible for the prevention, treatment, and rehabilitation of athletic injuries to collegiate athletes. In addition, the Athletic Trainer for Sports Medicine administers drug testing, insurance coordination, and travels with athletic teams to all events. The incumbent reports to the Associate AD Sports Medicine in the administration of a Division I intercollegiate Athletic program in adherence to all university and Kentucky Board of Medical Licensure regulations. Read more Part-Time Faculty, Managerial Communication 497519 Richmond Campus College of Business Part-Time Faculty The College of Business at Eastern Kentucky University invites applications for a part-time faculty position to teach courses in managerial communication. Read more Biology Student Tutor Fall 2026 497528 Richmond Campus College of Science, Tech, Eng & Math Student The Biological Sciences department is seeking undergraduate and graduate students to serve as tutors in the department's Peer Mentoring Center for the Fall 2026 semester. Students will be responsible for providing in-person and virtual tutoring in a one-on-one or group setting. Some evenings may be required. Previous tutoring experience is preferred but not required. Read more Part-Time Faculty, General Business 497520 Richmond Campus College of Business Part-Time Faculty The College of Business at Eastern Kentucky University invites applications for a part-time faculty position to teach courses in general business. Read more Part-Time Faculty, Marketing 497518 Richmond Campus College of Business Student Support Positions Part-Time Faculty The College of Business at Eastern Kentucky University invites applications for a part-time faculty position to teach courses in marketing. Read more Specialist, Master Fine Arts Program 497497 Richmond Campus College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sciences Part-Time Staff The MFA Program Specialist is responsible for staffing the Bluegrass Writers Studio office; creating and distributing marketing materials; maintaining the social media presence of the Bluegrass Writers Studio; updating the MFA student handbook; assisting the Program Director in arranging, preparing, and coordinating the domestic summer residency in July; assisting students with enrollment for the summer residency in Lisbon, Portugal; providing technical assistance to online graduate students; and serving as managing editor for the literary journal Jelly Bucket, including all aspects of production and distribution. Read more Director of Orchestral Studies 497425 Richmond Campus College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sciences Fulltime Faculty The School of Music, a unit of the Institute for Creative and Collaborative Arts at Eastern Kentucky University, invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track position as Director of Orchestral Studies, beginning 2027-28. Read more Part-Time Faculty, Communication 497502 Richmond Campus College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sciences Student Support Positions Part-Time Faculty Adjunct faculty are needed to teach face-to-face courses in Communication Studies, Broadcasting and Electronic Media (Film Techniques and Multimedia Journalism), and Public Relations at the Richmond campus. Read more Bursar 497412 Richmond Campus Financial Positions Fulltime Staff The Bursar provides strategic leadership and oversight for the institution’s student accounts, cashiering, collection, billing, and operations, ensuring the accuracy, integrity, and efficiency of all tuition, fee, and related financial transactions. This position plays a vital role in supporting the University’s administrative and student service functions through the timely and accurate billing, collection, and reconciliation of student accounts. Read more Model Lab School Girls' Varsity Basketball Head Coach 497455 Richmond Campus Model Lab School Positions Model Staff & Faculty Seasonal or Temporary Be a part of a winning girls' varsity basketball team in a world-class school environment as the Head Coach at Model Laboratory School. The Patriots have a rich heritage and a family atmosphere where teamwork is valued. Read more Part-Time Secondary Instructors, Dept. Chemistry and Forensic Science 497451 Richmond Campus College of Science, Tech, Eng & Math Student Support Positions Part-Time Faculty The Department of Chemistry and Forensic Science at EKU is seeking part-time Secondary Instructors to work with program faculty, assisting in teaching undergraduate lectures and laboratories. Appointments will begin this Fall 2026 semester, with options to renew on a semester-to-semester basis, as available. Read more Pest Control Technician 497446 Richmond Campus Skilled Craft Positions Fulltime Staff The Pest Control Technician serves as a utility worker within the Facilities Services Department, performing a combination of functions as needed to properly care for University property and service customers. These responsibilities can include: (1) Ensuring proper treatment and inspections of all university facilities and grounds as well as provision of emergency pest control. All other duties as assigned. Read more Flight Instructor (CFI) 497443 Other EKU Location College of Justice, Safety & Military Science Part-Time Staff Are you a CFI? Apply now! Read more Flight Instructor (CFII and/or MEI) 497444 Other EKU Location College of Justice, Safety & Military Science Part-Time Staff Are you a CFII and/or MEI? APPLY NOW!!!! Read more ICCA School of Art and Design Part-Time Faculty 497432 Richmond Campus College of Letters, Arts & Soc Sciences Student Support Positions Part-Time Faculty The ICCA School of Art and Design at Eastern Kentucky University invites applications for a part-time faculty position to teach courses in Art, Art History and Graphic Design. Courses may include, but are not limited to: Drawing, Two Dimensional Design, Three Dimensional Design, Digital Media, and Art Appreciation Read more Lab Technician, Aviation 497360 Other EKU Location College of Justice, Safety & Military Science Fulltime Staff The Lab Technician, Aviation supports the instructional and research missions of EKU’s School of Aviation by maintaining, calibrating, and repairing aviation laboratory equipment and facilities; preparing instructional aids and materials; ensuring safety and regulatory compliance; and assisting faculty and students in the proper use of tools, equipment, and learning resources. Read more Visiting Assistant Professor, Health Care Administration, Health Informatics and Information Management 497406 Richmond Campus College of Health Sciences Fulltime Faculty The Department of Environmental & Public Health, Administration, and Medical Sciences at Eastern Kentucky University invites applications for a non-tenure track Visiting Assistant Professor position in the Health Care Administration Program for Academic Year 2026-2027. Read more Workforce Education Instructor 497403 Richmond Campus Student Support Positions Part-Time Staff A Workforce Education Instructor is responsible for instruction, monitoring, and/or preparing curriculum for business/industry classes as well as grant programs. Read more Displaying 121 - 150 of 170 in total ‹ 1 2 3 4 5 6 › Equal Opportunity Eastern Kentucky University is an Equal Opportunity employer and educational institution and does not discriminate on the basis of age (40 and over), race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, gender expression, pregnancy, ethnicity, disability, national origin, veteran status, and/or genetic information in the admission to, or participation in, any educational program or activity (e.g., athletics, academics and housing) which it conducts, or in any employment policy or practice. Any complaint arising by reason of alleged discrimination should be directed to the Office of Equal Opportunity & Title IX, Eastern Kentucky University, Jones Bldg. Room 416, Richmond, Kentucky 40475 (859) 622-8020 , or the Assistant Secretary for Civil Rights, U.S. Department of Education, Office for Civil Rights, Lyndon Baines Johnson Department of Education Building, 400 Ma